{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/224619-what-do-you-think-a-hunter-the-vigil-chronicle-book-should-have","id":224619,"title":"What do you think a Hunter: The Vigil Chronicle book should have?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Hunter: The Vigil"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-08-10T16:39:43-07:00","id":224619,"title":"What do you think a Hunter: The Vigil Chronicle book should have?","content":"<span style=\"font-family:times new roman\">What do you think a Hunter: The Vigil Chronicle book should have? Personally, I would like to see those compacts and conspiracies rewritten. Maybe make 'em more, I dunno, customizable. We definitely need to update their tactics and endowments. </span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":729,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/729-ocel","user":"ocel","date":". 08-10-2014, 08:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/729-ocel","name":"ocel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"81"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-10T17:41:03-07:00","id":224669,"title":"","content":"More info on those alternative dimensions and more info about cults.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1873-jan-paparazzi","name":"Jan Paparazzi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1873_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"257"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-10T17:54:23-07:00","id":224678,"title":"","content":"I think it should have chronicle ideas about a bunch of hunters carrying out a vigil.<br /> <br /> Just a thought.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-10T17:56:02-07:00","id":224679,"title":"","content":"More on depth on how to customize, and more things for compacts to do, akin to compacts and conspiricies add on of powers for compacts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=392\" data-tempid=\"temp_392_1519878565794_106\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3676-manbearpig","name":"ManBearPig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3676_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"148"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-11T06:27:38-07:00","id":225036,"title":"","content":"I'd want it to emphasize the human nature of the Vigil. Really zoom in on the line between Civilians, Hunters, Slashers, and the interplay between those Hunters who are Sleepwalkers (and their equivalents) and those who are not.<br /> <br /> Also, what mentally differentiates a Mortal Hunter from a Supernatural who Hunts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Once is happenstance. Twice is coincidence. Three times is enemy action. Four times is Infrastructure.<br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><br /> Rule #2: Never let the game-mechanics get in the way of a good story.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1642-paddon","name":"Paddon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1642_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"326"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-11T13:01:34-07:00","id":225240,"title":"","content":"I would really like to see something like thekingsraven's work on divorcing the various aspects of Tier from the Compacts/Conspiracies, so that a small group could have Endowments or an international one could not. I'd also really appreciate monster templates (Bruiser, Mastermind, Stalker, etc) that we can throw Dread Powers on for quick monsters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-11T13:25:08-07:00","id":225259,"title":"","content":"I'm going to agree that Compacts and Conspiracies could use some work in a hypothetical Hunter chronicle. There should be a more clear distinction between what sets apart the two categories of organizations - the latter having access to full-sized Endowments isn't a very compelling or consistent reason, I think. Other than that, fully integrating the Code with Integrity as opposed to Morality is an obvious feature.<br /> <br /> Other than that, some new Merits might be nice, since Professional Training is no longer a &quot;Hunter thing&quot;. New Endowments, too. A lot of room for non-critical but fun content.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/186-morty","name":"Morty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar186_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-11T14:01:23-07:00","id":225299,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/224619-what-do-you-think-a-hunter-the-vigil-chronicle-book-should-have?p=225240#post225240\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would really like to see something like thekingsraven's work on divorcing the various aspects of Tier from the Compacts/Conspiracies, so that a small group could have Endowments or an international one could not. I'd also really appreciate monster templates (Bruiser, Mastermind, Stalker, etc) that we can throw Dread Powers on for quick monsters.</div> </div> </div> </div>Naturally I approve of any positive mention of my work <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> But I don't think a Chronicles book needs to go into quite the detail I did. I'd just have it out and out stated that Tier = the overall size and capabilities of an org; and has nothing to do with Endowments. You can have a Tier 3 group without any Endowments, and a Tier 2 group with Endowments (arguably the Lucifgue, Les Mysterys and Canites). Personally I'd say my qualifier for Tier 3 is &quot;given motivation can they get 100 armed men on the ground within one week?&quot; While Tier 2 is &quot;if you're on the ground, can you get nebulously defined 'support' in one week?&quot;. <br /> <br /> ================================================== =====================<br /> <br /> Now I'm done replying, here's I would say that the two big things I'd like to see are:<br /> <br /> <i>Less</i> of a core mood. Here me out before those first impressions get in. There are 12 core organisations and currently we have around 30 different organistaions. There's a lot of diversity, but I want to see even more diversity. The current core mood of feeling alone, ignorant and scared works great for Tier 1 play. It works great for The Union or The Long Night, but it's not an appropraite feeling for when TF:V are heading towards a Vampire's penthouse in a helicopter full of hellfire missiles, or when an AKD champion knocks on the door of a Consilia with The Spear of Lugh in hand (it's in Dream Catchers).<br /> <br /> <br /> Secondly, I want more focus on the organisations as actual organisations. Details on how they're organised internally, how demanding they are to their members. Support for using numbers, humanity's most potent advantage, and support for playing a high ranking officer.<br /> <br /> ================================================== ======================<br /> <br /> And now specific little things that I'd like.<br /> <br /> <br /> For Null Mysteriis: Three sidebars, it seems excessive but given how they've been handled in some of the books I think a strong explicit statement is necessary. The first simply explains that they believe in the supernatural and don't try to fit everything into the current real world scientific paradigm - even Rationalists believe &quot;it can be explained by science&quot;, not &quot;it fits into current models&quot;. The second says that they are often skeptics and that they're often right to do so &quot;Werewolves exist, but most large dog attacks are from actual dogs. So put down that shotgun until after I take a plaster cast of the bites&quot;. The third is the It's Decision Time sidebar from Compacts and Conspiracies.<br /> <br /> Ashwood Abbey: A bit less focus on the excess and a bit more focus on so called &quot;class&quot;. Most of all, it's about <i>novelty</i>. By the third drug fuelled orgy or the third fight with monsters they're bored. What haven't they done yet? Go fox-hunting in the spirit world with a pack of hired Werewolves in <i>Urhan</i>; dressed in classic English foxhunting gear, and track down fox spirits? Pay mad scientists to perform brain transplants and be the opposite sex for a while just to see what it's like?<br /> <br /> Aegis Kai Doru: Lets face it. They should have a stronger relationship to Mummies then they currently do. I always felt the focus on Werewolves was somewhat arbitary (they can't even use Werewolves' relics). I'd also like to play up their power and knowladge a bit. They have a real illuminati secret society vibe that I love; I'd like more oppotunities to play members who have bean taught occult lore and secret histories. Finally; the list of possible origins does not inlcude the possibility of being a Guardian of the Veil's Labarynth or a Mummy's Cult that went rogue. That must be fixed.<br /> <br /> VASCU &amp; Barret Comission. Add these to the core.<br /> <br /> Rules for Gods and Angels (non-God Machine). With the Long Night, the MM, the Knife of Paradise and the Lucifuge in the core hunter actually has some pretty strong themes of Abrahamic religion. It's also got some Netjerism in the Southern Temple (but they're more alchemists than polytheists). Now I'm not saying that God should exist in Hunter, or that he should be the guy behind Benedictions. What I'm saying is that if you say right there in the core book that you can play a Catholic priest with super-powered prayers; it's got to be a supported option for that to actually be Catholic-God answering those prayers. Same for the Lucifuge, if the first line says &quot;Satan&quot; you've got to support players who want to use the guy from the Bible/Datae's Inferno.<br /> <br /> Personally I'd like to see angels portrayed as terrifyingly powerful, if you're playing a Catholic priest, god's messengers should live up to your expectations. I'm thinking Rank 5, minimum.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-11T14:32:57-07:00","id":225316,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/224619-what-do-you-think-a-hunter-the-vigil-chronicle-book-should-have?p=225299#post225299\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>Less</i> of a core mood. Here me out before those first impressions get in. There are 12 core organisations and currently we have around 30 different organistaions. There's a lot of diversity, but I want to see even more diversity. The current core mood of feeling alone, ignorant and scared works great for Tier 1 play. It works great for The Union or The Long Night, but it's not an appropriate feeling for when TF:V are heading towards a Vampire's penthouse in a helicopter full of hellfire missiles, or when an AKD champion knocks on the door of a Consilia with The Spear of Lugh in hand (it's in Dream Catchers).<br /> <br /> <br /> Secondly, I want more focus on the organisations as actual organisations. Details on how they're organised internally, how demanding they are to their members. Support for using numbers, humanity's most potent advantage, and support for playing a high ranking officer.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm loving everything in your post, but this is my main one. Even if you're Tier 3, Hunter assumes that your cell is basically going to be a handful of largely-mundane people with little to no support and maybe a handful of Endowments to help you surive the night. That just doesn't make sense for VALKYRIE (who are a multinational military task force with a budget measured in the millions of dollars at minimum) or the AKD (who should feel like the Illuminati of the World of Darkness, rather than a few dudes with a magic trinket or two); if the player characters are part of a powerful, far-reaching, potentially ancient <i>conspiracy</i>, than it should feel like they actually belong to something.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-11T18:04:19-07:00","id":225480,"title":"","content":"Better mechanics for Tactics, better mechanics for creating your own Endowments. &quot;Endowment&quot; as it's own thing, as opposed to just being a Merit. I also would love a Vigil Chronicle book to be... just one big book for playing World of Darkness: Humans. Or near humans.<br /> <br /> I want rituals. Stuff like Abjuration, that technically anyone could do. I want to be like Sam and Dean and summon angels and demons with spells. I want to use rock salt shotguns and sigils scrawled in blood. <br /> I want a book that covers everything from cops and robbers to globe trotting McGuffin seeking. I want something that combines the best parts of all the &quot;blue book&quot; WoD games, only with the attention to detail and oversight that game lines get (because core WoD has some of the shittiest books, despite the good concepts; <i>Reliquary</i> and <i>Second Sight</i> are mechanically terrible. So is <i>Changing Breeds</i>).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my first Storyteller's Vault product: <a href=\"http://www.storytellersvault.com/product/438661/Pretty-Guardian-Faerie-Knights-A-Hunter-the-Vigil-Conspiracy\" target=\"_blank\">Pretty Guardian Faerie Knights</a><br /> Currently working on <b>Night Horrors: Pushing Daisies</b>. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1517001-%F0%9F%91%BB-a-handful-of-sample-geists\" target=\"_blank\">Sample here</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2998-aspel","name":"Aspel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2998_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"403"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-11T18:52:54-07:00","id":225535,"title":"","content":"Especially since GMC describes Supernatural stuff as a more &quot;in center&quot; thing (think of the Integrity questions), I think it would be a good idea for the devs to take a different look at what constitutes the Hunter template. I want to be able to go from &quot;Civilian&quot; to &quot;Hunter&quot; within a few sessions <i>without noticing</i>; I want the distinction to be that you chose <i>not</i> to forget.<br /> <br /> I want the Compacts and Conspiracies to just be Mystery Cults (or something similar); flesh out Mystery Cult a bunch to deal with this. I want to be able to represent the pencil-pushers as much as the front-end fighters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-11T19:49:33-07:00","id":225596,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aspel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/224619-what-do-you-think-a-hunter-the-vigil-chronicle-book-should-have?p=225480#post225480\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I also would love a Vigil Chronicle book to be... just one big book for playing World of Darkness: Humans. Or near humans.</div> </div> </div> </div>Like a NWOD Hunters Hunted?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-11T20:55:07-07:00","id":225626,"title":"","content":"I'd also love more support for chronicle models that aren't about murdering supernatural critters. Stuff like the VASCU (who have to arrest the monsters and give them a fair trial) or supernatural negotiators.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-12T00:32:55-07:00","id":225735,"title":"","content":"A couple more points I thought up:<br /> <br /> Cheiron - I'd like it to be clearer that the people involved are mostly good, and the perfectly mundane corporate beurocracy turns good intentions into evil results.<br /> <br /> Malleus Maleficarum - Get someone who knows Catholic theology, given how hard Onyx Path are working to make sure they portray different countries correctly it's kind of weird to still be seeing basic mistakes like calling Mummies a challenge to Catholic theology. <br /> <br /> In general there should be a hard rule that Hunter orgs intended for PCs should never be duped by the supernatural. I'm sure hunters do they fooled and subverted by the supernatural all the time, but the default assumption should be that PCs are not, and that you can play any org you like without breaking that assumption. Supernatural dupes can go in the antagonist chapter of Hunter (adding a section to The Enemy Within detailing alternative supernatural0subverted versions of the core orgs would be pretty cool) or other gamelines.<br /> <br /> I diversity rule saying that in every book using the standard 3 Compacts + 1 Conspiracy format there can be at most one group that hunts out of ignorance &amp; prejudice and at least one group with a goal unrelated to killing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-12T04:41:29-07:00","id":225825,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/224619-what-do-you-think-a-hunter-the-vigil-chronicle-book-should-have?p=225626#post225626\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd also love more support for chronicle models that aren't about murdering supernatural critters. Stuff like the VASCU (who have to arrest the monsters and give them a fair trial) or supernatural negotiators.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, agreed. Non-violent interaction with monsters could use more emphasis. It's already mentioned and supported, mind you, but fighting supernaturals is still given prominence. Witchfinders suffers from it in particular, I think.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":186,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/186-morty","user":"Morty","date":". 08-12-2014, 07:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/186-morty","name":"Morty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar186_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-12T08:15:28-07:00","id":225982,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:times new roman\">Yeah, I don't want the Invictus funding Task Force Valkyrie or a ghoul running the Longious branch of the </span><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\">Malleus </span><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\">Maleficarum anymore either. I'm cool with them manipulating chapter houses of those organizations though. Y'know, there was this post JTory made awhile back, talking about how to make TF:V independent and whatnot. Maybe we can build on that, think of ways to free other compacts and conspiracies of their insert supernatural template here overlords. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/13184-c-c-tfv-and-vampires?p=21071#post21071\">Here's the link for it.</a><br /> Crazy idea: Why not make some of those compacts a part of a larger organization? They could be a confederation of compacts that share a common interest like lodges, unions, institutes, syndicates, communities, faithful, et cetera.</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":729,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/729-ocel","user":"ocel","date":". 08-12-2014, 01:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/729-ocel","name":"ocel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"81"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-12T09:53:57-07:00","id":226053,"title":"","content":"I actually don't mind having a Ghoul in charge; I consider anything without a modified Integrity trait to be human and he always struck me as genuinely dedicated to the MM's official goals - with a little skimming blood off the top as well.<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ocel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/224619-what-do-you-think-a-hunter-the-vigil-chronicle-book-should-have?p=225982#post225982\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Crazy idea: Why not make some of those compacts a part of a larger organization? They could be a confederation of compacts that share a common interest like lodges, unions, institutes, syndicates, communities, faithful, et cetera.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would very much like to see it explicitly stated that there's lots of different Unions, and we're just shown a typical example.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 08-12-2014, 12:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-12T12:04:00-07:00","id":226180,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ocel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/224619-what-do-you-think-a-hunter-the-vigil-chronicle-book-should-have?p=225982#post225982\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\">Yeah, I don't want the Invictus funding Task Force Valkyrie or a ghoul running the Longious branch of the </span><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\">Malleus </span><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\">Maleficarum anymore either. I'm cool with them manipulating chapter houses of those organizations though. Y'know, there was this post JTory made awhile back, talking about how to make TF:V independent and whatnot. Maybe we can build on that, think of ways to free other compacts and conspiracies of their insert supernatural template here overlords. <a href=\"https://&amp;quot;&#91;url\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/13184-c-c-tfv-and-vampires?p=21071#post21071&amp;quot;]Here's</a> the link for it.[/URL]</span></div> </div> </div> </div>I stand by my crazy headcanon for VALKYRIE; that Cheiron funds them in exchange for all the monster bodies they end up with. It's a nice supernatural twist on the military-industrial corporate complex that plagues mundane America already.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-12T20:39:16-07:00","id":226750,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/224619-what-do-you-think-a-hunter-the-vigil-chronicle-book-should-have?p=225299#post225299\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Aegis Kai Doru: Lets face it. They should have a stronger relationship to Mummies then they currently do.</div> </div> </div> </div>You know, there's this thing in comedy where the artists go through and find all the obvious jokes they can make?<br /> <br /> And then throw them out, because <i>everyone</i> already knows the obvious jokes. They're dull.<br /> <br /> I feel this way about making Mummies the main enemies for the Guardians. Besides, it's much more satisfying for the Ascending Ones to take that group.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Plus AKD Has that entire Greco-Roman theme-ing and the Cult of the Phoenix has that Middle Eastern theme-ing going on.<br /> <br /> BACK TO THE ORIGINAL POST: On a related note, can someone please remind the Shadow Congregation that they don't just hunt vampires, but mages and demons too?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 08-13-2014, 12:01 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-12T20:47:20-07:00","id":226759,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/224619-what-do-you-think-a-hunter-the-vigil-chronicle-book-should-have?p=225735#post225735\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In general there should be a hard rule that Hunter orgs intended for PCs should never be duped by the supernatural. I'm sure hunters do they fooled and subverted by the supernatural all the time, but the default assumption should be that PCs are not, and that you can play any org you like without breaking that assumption. Supernatural dupes can go in the antagonist chapter of Hunter (adding a section to The Enemy Within detailing alternative supernatural0subverted versions of the core orgs would be pretty cool) or other gamelines.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am of the opinion you are missing the point hardcore.<br /> <br /> But I've done that song and dance before, and I think, ultimately, that's going to be one of those things they don't touch, so I'll leave it at &quot;Who cares?&quot;.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-13T01:22:42-07:00","id":226840,"title":"","content":"Character creation: this should be mechanically identical to the character creation rules in <b>World of Darkness</b>, as modified by the GMC rules update. There should be no \u201cstep five: apply the hunter template\u201d, because there should be nothing in there to give the impression that hunters have a template. The <i>only</i> difference between mortal character creation and hunter character creation should be what sorts of questions are asked at step one (background) and what sorts of options are available at step seven (Merits). <br /> <br /> Tiers: I like The King\u2019s Raven\u2019s notion that the difference between Compacts and Conspiracies is how organized you are, and I agree with the notion of divorcing Endowments from Conspiracies. I also like the notion that some groups that have been labeled as Conspiracies should be reclassified as Compacts. <br /> <br /> OTOH, I also don\u2019t think that \u201ctier\u201d should be used as a synonym for \u201ccells, compacts, or conspiracies\u201d. Rather, Tiers should be described in terms of intended play-style:<br /> <br /> \u2022 <i>Tier One</i> is for those Storytellers who like the notion that hunters are no different from regular mortals, save only for the fact that they take a proactive stance when it comes to monsters. By definition, games played on this Tier don\u2019t feature any special rules that regular mortals don\u2019t have access to; nor do the hunters have any exemptions from any rules that work against ordinary mortals (e.g., Lunacy or the Lie). Practical Experience and Tactics are pretty much the only rules options that are suggested for Tier One play; and even then, they\u2019re only <i>suggested</i>: it\u2019s perfectly reasonable to run a Tier One game where the only special rules involved are the monster rules. <br /> <br /> \u2022 <i>Tier Two</i> assumes that the protagonists are something special, though not supernatural. Practical Experience, Tactics, and Risking Willpower are recommended at this Tier of play. Also at this Tier of play, I\u2019d suggest a new (to <b>Hunter</b>) option of Boosts, inspired by <b>Strange Dead Love</b>\u2019s Heroic Mortals, which amount to more ways to spend Practical Experience: Attribute Boosts, Advantage Boosts (e.g., Defense, Health, Initiative, and Speed), and what I call Edges (options that let you do more with a trait such as Willpower, Integrity, or Skills than the normal rules allow). Edges would include such things as the Extended Willpower rules from <b>Mirrors</b> (i.e., more ways to spend Willpower), the Skill Tricks from <b>Mirrors</b> (more ways to use Skills), and immunity to the likes of Lunacy, the Lie, or Disquiet. None of the Boosts would be inherently supernatural, though; and each would describe not just its mechanical effects, but what sort of impact allowing it in the game would have. <br /> <br /> \u2022 <i>Tier Three</i> assumes that the lines between mortal and monster have been blurred, and that hunters have reason to question which side of that line they stand on. Supernatural Merits (such as Endowments) are recommended at this tier of play, and Conviction from <b>Mirrors</b> becomes an option. <br /> <br /> Note the terminology I\u2019ve been using: \u201crecommendations\u201d are things that are assumed to be available unless the Storyteller specifically says otherwise; \u201coptions\u201d are only available if the Storyteller specifically allows them. That is, recommendations are opt-out; options are opt-in. <br /> <br /> Cells, Compacts, and Conspiracies: due to how <b>Hunter</b> was originally conceived, Cells and Compacts have been set up for what I\u2019m calling Tier Two play (sans options), while Conspiracies have been set up for Tier Three play. Some of this lock-step nature can be addressed by downgrading some Conspiracies to Compacts (resulting in there being some Compacts designed with Tier Three play in mind); but I\u2019d like the Chronicle book to go further and suggest ways that (what are currently Conspiracies) could be used in Tier Two or even Tier One games, or how Compacts or independent Cells could be adapted for use in Tier Three games. Not everyone in the Malleus Maleficatorum has studied Benedictions; and you could get some solid Tier One or Two play out of a cell of hunters from that Conspiracy who <i>can\u2019t</i> call down miracles. <br /> <br /> In short, I\u2019d like Hunter to feature a highly customizable experience.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 08-13-2014, 04:26 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-13T04:02:35-07:00","id":226897,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:times new roman\">I don't think Hunters should be immune to Lunacy, Blood Bonding, Disquiet or what have you, Conviction less so, 'cause we already have a code for that, but I do agree with everything else you've said, </span><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\">Dataweaver. We could take a page from the idigam chronicle and have players make a couple of characters on the side, each one a member or supporter of the cell, much like making a pack in werewolf.</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":729,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/729-ocel","user":"ocel","date":". 08-13-2014, 07:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/729-ocel","name":"ocel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"81"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-13T04:32:57-07:00","id":226907,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"font-family:times new roman\">Maybe we should </span><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\">take a page from the idigam chronicle and make cells like packs.</span> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><br /> <br /> In what sense? I haven't really been following IC.</span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-13T04:39:15-07:00","id":226911,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:times new roman\">I was referring to a Werewolf the Forsaken: Idigam Chronicle preview called The Gang's All Here. <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/the-gangs-all-here/\" target=\"_blank\">Here's the link.</a> I apologize for not putting up a link to it in my last post.</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":729,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/729-ocel","user":"ocel","date":". 08-13-2014, 07:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/729-ocel","name":"ocel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"81"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-13T04:51:50-07:00","id":226914,"title":"","content":"I also like Dataweaver's ideas; they would make Hunter much more customizable while also retaining what's possible in it now. As far as Lunacy, the Lie and Disquiet go, I think the immunization to their effects should be gradual rather than simply 'flipping a switch'. And I don't think resistance to Disquiet is appropriate in any circumstances. Its insidious and inescapable nature is rather important. Of course, the transition between Tier One and Tier Two in such a paradigm should definitely be allowed to occur in play - hunters start out as scared, confused people standing up to something they don't understand, but the sheer weight of what they've seen and done eventually sets them apart from other mortals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/186-morty","name":"Morty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar186_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-13T04:57:21-07:00","id":226918,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ocel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/224619-what-do-you-think-a-hunter-the-vigil-chronicle-book-should-have?p=226897#post226897\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think Hunters should be immune to Lunacy, Blood Bonding, Disquite and so on, or have Conviction, 'cause we have the code for that, but I do agree with everything else you've said, Dataweaver.</div> </div> </div> </div>There\u2019s a reason why I described those items strictly as \u201copt-in\u201d things that are only to be used if the Storyteller wants to use them; and why I also suggested that they be accompanied by clear statements of the consequences of allowing them, so that nobody can say that they weren\u2019t warned if it goes south on them. But if you check out <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/217641-the-lie-and-the-vigil\">The Lie and the Vigil</a>, you\u2019ll find someone arguing for why hunters who are a cut above the average mortal (which is what my proposed Tier Two is all about) shouldn\u2019t be subject to the Lie; and you\u2019ll find someone else arguing that being a Sleepwalker (i.e., not subject to the Lie) is a more natural state for humans and that becoming a Sleepwalker isn\u2019t a supernatural change. That\u2019s the sort of gaming group that the Edges involving Lunacy, the Lie, and Disquiet are intended to cater to. <br /> <br /> (Note also that I didn\u2019t mention Blood Bonding; that\u2019s partially because I\u2019m not terribly familiar with <b>Vampire</b>, and partially because what I <i>do</i> know of Blood Bonding doesn\u2019t strike me as being the same sort of thing as the others: as I understand it, <i>nobody</i> gets immunity to Blood Bonding, not even vampires.)<br /> <br /> Likewise, you\u2019ll note that I listed Conviction as an \u201copt-in\u201d thing for Tier Three, where the line between mortal and monster blurs: <i>I</i> don\u2019t consider it to be a supernatural thing; but I\u2019m well aware that there are others who do. I think it fits perfectly in the gray area that Tier Three games represent; but it should <i>only</i> be used if the Storyteller wants to use it. In particular, it\u2019s not something that should show up on published Storyteller characters, any more than Tier Two\u2019s Boost options should.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/224619-what-do-you-think-a-hunter-the-vigil-chronicle-book-should-have?p=226914#post226914\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I also like Dataweaver's ideas; they would make Hunter much more customizable while also retaining what's possible in it now. As far as Lunacy, the Lie and Disquiet go, I think the immunization to their effects should be gradual rather than simply 'flipping a switch'.</div> </div> </div> </div>Perhaps; I\u2019m not averse to the notion of immunity being preceded by resistance. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/224619-what-do-you-think-a-hunter-the-vigil-chronicle-book-should-have?p=226914#post226914\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And I don't think resistance to Disquiet is appropriate in any circumstances. Its insidious and inescapable nature is rather important.</div> </div> </div> </div>Again, list the consequences of each option so the Storyteller can make an informed decision. And there <i>are</i> mortals who are immune to Disquiet (e.g., some of the luckier among the Redeemed); so it\u2019s not like granting such immunity is without precedent. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/224619-what-do-you-think-a-hunter-the-vigil-chronicle-book-should-have?p=226914#post226914\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Of course, the transition between Tier One and Tier Two in such a paradigm should definitely be allowed to occur in play - hunters start out as scared, confused people standing up to something they don't understand, but the sheer weight of what they've seen and done eventually sets them apart from other mortals.</div> </div> </div> </div>Transitioning down the Tiers would harder to justify, though, as it would involve <i>giving up</i> options that had previously been available. Going from tier three to tier two play would likely involve losing any Endowments the hunters have, because Endowments are a Tier Three thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 08-13-2014, 09:33 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-13T07:55:30-07:00","id":227023,"title":"","content":"I'm very much in favor of the Tier ideas expressed above and would, in fact, be in favor of going just a bit further. Instead of Tiers merely representing the scope of select organizations, I think it'd be neat if the book contained rules for modifying the existing compacts and conspiracies to fit that level of scope. <br /> <br /> For example: VASCU. Tier 1 &quot;The Basement&quot; (VASCU consists of a Cell of FBI Hunters working X-files like cases) &gt;&gt; Tier 2 VASCU as written &gt;&gt; Tier 3 &quot;The Vanguard&quot; (VASCU as an international Interpol-like organization given their mandate by the UN, maybe spun off even more from the Society of the Twelve Keys). <br /> <br /> Also, regarding a Hunter Chronicle Book, I think it'd be neat if it tackled the transformation of human into monster (ideologically and/or supernaturally), particularly if said transformation was a byproduct of a corruption of the Vigil. I think I'd call it the Contagion Chronicles and showcase the Vigil as something of a &quot;force,&quot; although not characterized like the Principle or the Abyss. This Vigil gives Mortals who strike back against the supernatural a slight push unavailable to other Mortals in the form of Risking Willpower and maybe some slight bonuses when resisting Lunacy and the Lie (I'd probably have Hunters, in general, lump all the &quot;forgetting&quot; effects together into one concept called The Bystander Effect, or The Effect for short). However, the Vigil has a dark side to it in that it is easily contaminated by the supernatural, causing Hunters who too carelessly &quot;use the devils tools against him&quot; to slowly, painfully, and maddeningly cross the line from human into... something else. Fight fire with fire too often and soon the whole world will burn. <br /> <br /> Love, Peace, and Chicken Grease,<br /> The Mighty Grendel","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1931-the-mighty-grendel","name":"The Mighty Grendel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1931_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-13T10:01:18-07:00","id":227088,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:times new roman\">Ah yes, I've read that thread and think you and Joker are on to something.<br /> Sleepers have one advantage their awakened counterparts don't: Paradox. A wizard may try to bend us mere mortals to his will, but like a rubber band, we'll bounce back with a vengeance, likely poking that fool's eye out in the process. Further more, a sleeper doesn't have to be a hunter to hunt the supernatural. Take the police for instance, a magician may be questioned for being at the scene of the crime/freak incident. If he's caught lying, they'll hold him accountable for that crime. If he tells them the truth, they'll throw him into an insane asylum. If he tries to use sorcery to get out of this mess... well at that point, he's probably too far gone to help now. Note that this is a gross oversimplification of the point I'm trying to get across.<br /> I'd like to see this after action report tactic expanded upon.<br /> Has anyone thought of making willpower into a sort of pseudo power stat for hunters? It could be used to resist supernatural things like lie induced amnesia and whatnot. In order to activate it, the player must risk one of his character's willpower dots, and roll the rest.</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":729,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/729-ocel","user":"ocel","date":". 08-13-2014, 03:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/729-ocel","name":"ocel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"81"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-13T10:09:18-07:00","id":227112,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/224619-what-do-you-think-a-hunter-the-vigil-chronicle-book-should-have?p=226840#post226840\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Character creation: this should be mechanically identical to the character creation rules in <b>World of Darkness</b>, as modified by the GMC rules update. There should be no \u201cstep five: apply the hunter template\u201d, because there should be nothing in there to give the impression that hunters have a template. The <i>only</i> difference between mortal character creation and hunter character creation should be what sorts of questions are asked at step one (background) and what sorts of options are available at step seven (Merits).</div> </div> </div> </div>While I have no real objection to making a Tier play based on the intended charachter style; I would want it to be in addition to rather than in place of the general size/power/&quot;organized-ness&quot; of the group.<br /> <br /> To put it another way; I think the difference between three guys alone against the darkness, and three guys alone against the darkness with Castigation is smaller than the difference between three guys alone against the darkness and three guys with no unique mechanics but they're army special forces piloting an apache gunship; with teams of analysts giving them intel and lots of backup.<br /> <br /> Plus, strength in numbers is closer to the thematic core of Hunter than Castigation.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/224619-what-do-you-think-a-hunter-the-vigil-chronicle-book-should-have?p=226750#post226750\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You know, there's this thing in comedy where the artists go through and find all the obvious jokes they can make?<br /> <br /> And then throw them out, because <i>everyone</i> already knows the obvious jokes. They're dull.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fortunately conspiracy design is not about humour. Obviousness isn't bad, and AKD's mummy links isn't just a possibility, it's an inevitability. The two groups have identical goals - acquiring relics, they're been fighting a large chunk of history. That is going to get into their collective culture.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-13T10:31:13-07:00","id":227131,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/224619-what-do-you-think-a-hunter-the-vigil-chronicle-book-should-have?p=227112#post227112\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> While I have no real objection to making a Tier play based on the intended charachter style; I would want it to be in addition to rather than in place of the general size/power/&amp;quot;organized-ness&amp;quot; of the group.<br /> <br /> To put it another way; I think the difference between three guys alone against the darkness, and three guys alone against the darkness with Castigation is smaller than the difference between three guys alone against the darkness and three guys with no unique mechanics but they're army special forces piloting an apache gunship; with teams of analysts giving them intel and lots of backup.<br /> <br /> Plus, strength in numbers is closer to the thematic core of Hunter than Castigation.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, certainly; I\u2019m fine with keeping the cell/compact/conspiracy distinction, with the defining element being how large and organized the org is. I just don\u2019t think you need to use the term \u201ctier\u201d to make that distinction, and there are better uses for it. <br /> <br /> As for the thematic core, each Tier has its own thematic core: \u201cstrength in numbers\u201d is more of a Tier Two thing than a Tier Three thing, where the thematic core seems to be closer to \u201cAm I a Man or a Muppet?\u201d (err\u2026 Monster?) The Lucifuge are Tier Three all the way: it doesn\u2019t matter how well- or poorly-organized they are; their defining characteristic is that they have demonic overtones.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-13T11:46:45-07:00","id":227169,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/224619-what-do-you-think-a-hunter-the-vigil-chronicle-book-should-have?p=226918#post226918\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(Note also that I didn\u2019t mention Blood Bonding; that\u2019s partially because I\u2019m not terribly familiar with <b>Vampire</b>, and partially because what I <i>do</i> know of Blood Bonding doesn\u2019t strike me as being the same sort of thing as the others: as I understand it, <i>nobody</i> gets immunity to Blood Bonding, not even vampires.)</div> </div> </div> </div>I could see some people being more resistant to Blood Bonding than others, but in general, it should be a very rare thing. Vampiric Vitae is potent when ingested. And from another point of view, it's less common than the Lie, Lunacy or Disquiet - you need to actually ingest the Vitae for blood bonding to take hold, whereas the other three effects happen every time a mortal human sees a Supernal spell, a werewolf's bestial form or interacts with a Promethean.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Perhaps; I\u2019m not averse to the notion of immunity being preceded by resistance. </div> </div> </div>Outright immunity should be reserved for supernatually touched mortals, like Sleepwalkers or Wolf-Blooded. Normal people should be able to push through those effects with effort - Tier Two hunters with noticeably less effort than Tier One, in this case.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Again, list the consequences of each option so the Storyteller can make an informed decision. And there <i>are</i> mortals who are immune to Disquiet (e.g., some of the luckier among the Redeemed); so it\u2019s not like granting such immunity is without precedent. </div> </div> </div>True, there are different views on Disquiet and the nWoD is nothing if not modular.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Transitioning down the Tiers would harder to justify, though, as it would involve <i>giving up</i> options that had previously been available. Going from tier three to tier two play would likely involve losing any Endowments the hunters have, because Endowments are a Tier Three thing. </div> </div> </div>How likely losing Endowments is depends on the organization in question; someone who leaves TFV without being court-martialled and locked away somewhere will lose access to its resources, and a Malleus Maleficarum member might suffer a crisis of faith that'll leave her unable to use Benedictions. But a Lucifuge member is unlikely to lose the Castigations. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/186-morty","name":"Morty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar186_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-13T12:01:05-07:00","id":227212,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/224619-what-do-you-think-a-hunter-the-vigil-chronicle-book-should-have?p=227131#post227131\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for the thematic core, each Tier has its own thematic core: \u201cstrength in numbers\u201d is more of a Tier Two thing than a Tier Three thing, where the thematic core seems to be closer to \u201cAm I a Man or a Muppet?\u201d (err\u2026 Monster?) The Lucifuge are Tier Three all the way: it doesn\u2019t matter how well- or poorly-organized they are; their defining characteristic is that they have demonic overtones.</div> </div> </div> </div>TF:V being the obvious counterpoint. But I would actually say that strength in numbers is the core cross-tier theme or rather I'd quote from the origonal development blogs at you; (with Tier 1 interpereting it as &quot;numbers is strength, we don't have numbers. Oh crap&quot;); it's just that Tier 3 has been handled the theme pretty badly so it doesn't give that impression.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-13T13:06:44-07:00","id":227282,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/224619-what-do-you-think-a-hunter-the-vigil-chronicle-book-should-have?p=227112#post227112\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Fortunately conspiracy design is not about humour. Obviousness isn't bad, and AKD's mummy links isn't just a possibility, it's an inevitability. The two groups have identical goals - acquiring relics, they're been fighting a large chunk of history. That is going to get into their collective culture.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wow. I woke up this morning reflecting a little on how lazy my response and thinking that nothing could be lazier, and then I read &quot;Fortunately conspiracy design is not about humour&quot;.<br /> <br /> Well, I feel better about the initial statement. Granted, you did go and support it, but still..well, again, I think some of the point is missed. I think a lot of the point was missed.<br /> <br /> I mean, don't get me wrong: <i>of course</i> these guys are enemies. Of course they butt heads. But by and large, that's because their surface elements run similar to one another, as a matter of incidence.<br /> <br /> But as thematics go, mummies just don't tap into the entire 'paradise lost' thing the AKD have as their core, which is why their enemies are mages and werewolves as well as why their endowments are relics.<br /> <br /> See, that's the thing that's all over the place, this sentiment that <i>we've lost heights unimaginable, and are left with naught but shadows, and all responsible will pay</i>. Out of...well, all the conspiracies, really, the two oldest are the Aegis Kai Doru and the Ascending Ones. But where the Ascending Ones claim roots in one of the oldest civilizations of the world, the AKD claim older, and they have perpetually described the first world as paradisical. The fact the world isn't is where their oath comes from, and everything the AKD does reflects a broken world where they have to make do with the pieces. They don't have magic of their own, they have to play with the shards of magic found in stuff(relics)-which at least isn't tainted in some form or fashion, like just about every other form of Endowment out there in Hunter, but still, people lack inherent magic(innate sleepwalker status, if you will, tying into FWC), and the world is not as it should be, there are divides and wounds in the entire cosmology. And who sits pretty at the heart of the explosion?<br /> <br /> Mages, inherently. Mages still <i>have </i>magic, and boy isn't that unfair. Mages speak about the fractured divide between the heights and here and they talk about it being the fault of their ancestors,and the concepts they play with seem to speak to the divide. It doesn't take long interacting with them to realize they deserve all the shit.<br /> <br /> Werewolves are less inherent, but the way they explain things makes it just as clear: humanity's fallen state is their fault as well. THese guys are primal, and their stories just as much so, and the more they explain their duty and sense of morality and why they have it, the more and more it becomes apparent that they are moved, mythologically, by the destruction of the first world, and they claim their ancestors had to do it.<br /> <br /> On top of that, both sides seem to propagate the fracture. Spirit and Flesh weren't once so divided, but the Werewolves, on top of rending a gash in the seperation, actively seek to make things even more separate(from the AKD's point of view, anyways). Mages recklessly use their gifts, that they deny most of humanity, and in their recklessness they rip the fabric of reality and introduce dark things from beyond, tearing apart the world. Yeah, these guys need to be hunted down. They need to be punished, and ideally removed, so that the at the least things don't get worst. Even if they don't make things worse, at least by killing them off you will have avenged the whole of humanity.<br /> <br /> Mummies are also symbols of things getting fucked up, but conversations with them don't lead to a changing of the fundamental nature of the world. They may have screwed with civilizations, but they aren't responsible for the divide that Mages and Werewolves seem to be. So while mummies are annoying for eating the magic of the world and denying the AKD even their broken glass pieces of a higher world, at the very least they aren't walking testaments to a fallen world. The Guardian's issue with them is more business-like than it is with most- you hate them for the struggle of resources, but not on an ideological level.<br /> <br /> And by the way: Yes, this isn't humor, but funnily enough, horror and comedy play on the same principles a lot. And Hell, good storytelling is a mix between the inevitable and the twists. A straight &quot;Oh, they both go after relics,revise the oath and themes to fit that&quot; is boring. It is <i>so boring</i>. What they've done with AKD is far more interesting, more dynamic, and stronger on a thematic level that makes the organization vivid and alive rather than just an item on a checklist.<br /> <br /> Mummies as a frequent opponent? Sure. Mummies as part of the Oath? Fuck no.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-13T14:27:14-07:00","id":227343,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> TF:V being the obvious counterpoint. </div> </div> </div>Technically yes, but metaphorically I'd say no. They're extra-judicial death squads commanded by unknown people (for the characters at least) for unknown purposes. TFV asks the question of whether you're actually fighting against the conspiracies that choke the WoD or have you simply joined one of those conspiracies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-13T14:57:54-07:00","id":227366,"title":"","content":"Hm. I've always seen the focus on both Mages <i>and </i>Werewolves on part of the Aegis Kai Doru rather weird and arbitrary, but I suppose it kind of makes sense when you explain it this way. Both kinds have a backstory that may or may not be true, but either way, it can be interpreted as &quot;the world was a paradise, now it's a shithole, and it's <i>their damn fault</i>&quot;. It fits a Hunter group centred around scavenging bits and pieces of lost power from aeons past. I believe both the myth of Atlantis and Pangaea will be less prominent in the Fallen World Chronicle and Idigam Chronicle, but it's not like it has to stop AKD.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/186-morty","name":"Morty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar186_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-13T15:00:21-07:00","id":227367,"title":"","content":"Arc, I have to disagree, not with the core concept you have here, but with the underlying evidence you're using to support your point. Basically, you're saying &quot;Werewolves because paradise lost.&quot; I think that Mummies have a far bigger paradise lost theme than Werewolves.<br /> <br /> Yes the First Pack's sin, if taken as truth, did far more damage to the world than anything the Iremites did. But in contrast Irem is far more important to Mummies than Father Wolf's death is to the Forsaken. The core of a standard Werewolf game is taking some territory and guarding it. The core of a Mummy game is remembering your past, your Iremite past. In addition Mummies spend tons of time finding ways to honor Irem in the modern world or make the modern world more like Irem.<br /> <br /> I think that what the survivors are doing today matters far more for a &quot;paradise lost&quot; theme than the scale of the cataclysm.<br /> <br /> <br /> Next I point out that I actually didn't like the way the &quot;paradise lost&quot; theme was handled in the current AKD. 90% of it's actual effects can be boiled down to &quot;kill Witches and Werewolves&quot; It felt small minded and petty, in a Conspiracy that should be about the grand sweap of history. I don't want them to be focused on revenge for an ancient grudge, I want them to have big proactive plans that tie back to their lost paradise. Plans to rebuild it. Plans to rediscover lost historys. Legends of specific relics from the old world that they want to recover. Heck, you could say that they only care about monsters because they're in their way. Their theme of paradise lost has potential, turning it into yet another example of &quot;we hate those monsters&quot; wastes that potential.<br /> <br /> And, well, the Mage setting and the Mummy setting are full of opportunities for grand Archeology/Relic themed plans to change the world. The Werewolf setting is not. Pick Mage, pick Mummy, pick neither. But just make whatever choice leads to big plans - that choice is not Werewolf.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> In summery. I believe that Mummy is a better fit for the Paradise Lost theme, a better fit for the archeology theme, and most importantly it's setting provides more opportunities for the AKD to be proactive with their goals. In contrast Werewolf has a Paradise Lost as backstory but not a theme, and little opportunity for archeology or the AKD to be proactive in anything other than killing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-13T15:21:21-07:00","id":227375,"title":"","content":"Irem has never been described as a paradise and Mummies seem pretty willing to tell you that if you ask; they honour it because it's their home. Further, it wasn't really 'lost', it seems to have served it's purpose, whatever that was.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-13T15:24:51-07:00","id":227376,"title":"","content":"Neither was Atlantis or Pangaea (at least not for humans).<br /> <br /> There's also plenty of Mages who'll tell you Atlantis probably wasn't perfect or didn't even exist. I don't think many Werewolves care one way or another how nice Pangaia was.<br /> <br /> And Atlantis &quot;served it's purpose&quot; in the exact way that Irem did - it created the tools needed for the big ritual that destroyed it. The only difference is that Mages complain about the guys behind the ritual more than Mummies.<br /> <br /> <br /> Really, the only true &quot;Paradise Lost&quot; was the fact the Abyss (probably) didn't exist in ancient times. Unless you count Princess; the AKD are Princesss afilliated now ;p","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 08-13-2014, 06:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-13T16:02:17-07:00","id":227388,"title":"","content":"On a more meta-level; the AKD are supernatural archaeologists. They collect magical <i>stuff</i> from around the globe. Mages have lots of artifacts and Mummies* have lots of artifacts, so they fit well as primary antagonists. *Mummies don't actually just <i>have</i> artifacts, they actively hunt for them and hoard them. It's nonsensical to not have them cross paths with the AKD more than any other supernatural group. <br /> <br /> TRYING TO PUT THIS DEBATE ASIDE FOR A MOMENT, I think <i>Hunter</i> needs more unique antagonists. The novelty of vampires, werewolves, and mages can quickly wear off for folks who have been romping around in the supernatural sandbox of the World of Darkness for a number of years. Throwing in some fresh new monsters that don't have easy analogues from other gamelines means that players can actually be as clueless as their characters for once, and have a fun time actually looking for weaknesses rather than trying to find fire/silver/cold iron/etc.<br /> <br /> I'd also love to divorce Tier from Compact/Conspiracy. A VALKYRIE cell should just as easily be a single fireteam that hears from their higher-ups every once in a blue moon for a Night at the Opera (Tier 1) as they are a jet-setting group of international military troubleshooters (Tier 3). Tier is essential to Hunter play and I'd like as many of the groups as possible to function at all levels.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-13T22:14:28-07:00","id":227584,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/224619-what-do-you-think-a-hunter-the-vigil-chronicle-book-should-have?p=227388#post227388\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">TRYING TO PUT THIS DEBATE ASIDE FOR A MOMENT, I think <i>Hunter</i> needs more unique antagonists. The novelty of vampires, werewolves, and mages can quickly wear off for folks who have been romping around in the supernatural sandbox of the World of Darkness for a number of years. Throwing in some fresh new monsters that don't have easy analogues from other gamelines means that players can actually be as clueless as their characters for once, and have a fun time actually looking for weaknesses rather than trying to find fire/silver/cold iron/etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>I\u2019d love to see the Monsters mechanics from <b>Mortal Remains</b> incorporated into the <b>Hunter</b> Chronicle Book, up to and including its advice on how to make your own templates; I\u2019d also like to see the \u201cAntagonists\u201d section of the Chronicle Book include a sample write-up for at least one monster who doesn\u2019t fit any of the standard templates \u2014 say, the Moth Man from one of the <b>World of Darkness</b>\u2019 introductory fiction pieces. <br /> <br /> One of the things I loved about <b>Night Stalkers</b> and <b>Spirit Slayers</b> in particular,and also in <b>Witch Finders</b> to a lesser extent, is that their monster sections didn\u2019t try to mimic the basis gameline\u2019s protagonists too closely: e.g., <b>Night Stalkers</b> let you make a variety of different kinds of vampires, most of whom were substantially different from the Kindred. One of my disappointments with <b>Mortal Remains</b> was that this aspect of things tended to get lost: for instance, the chapter on Prometheans didn\u2019t read like wild speculation on the many different kinds of artificial beings that might show up in the WoD; rather, it read more like a beta test of the rules for the Promethean Chronicle book. I\u2019d like to see the Hunter Chronicle book rectify that by presenting at least starting points for alternate takes on each of the standard monster types: rather than focusing in on how to more closely mimic the inspiring gameline\u2019s protagonists, \u201cblur the lens\u201d to encourage the Storyteller to try different takes on them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-14T02:18:11-07:00","id":227716,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Neither was Atlantis </div> </div> </div>That's the basic foundational ideology of the Diamond orders. It's their myth of a golden age when everything was better, however they choose to define 'better'. That's why it compares better to Irem. Irem was a Bronze Age slave empire, Atlantis was pretty much whatever you want it to be.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And Atlantis &quot;served it's purpose&quot; in the exact way that Irem did - it created the tools needed for the big ritual that destroyed it. </div> </div> </div>No it didn't. Atlantis sank when the Ladder was deliberately shattered. No one intended to destroy Atlantis as well. (at least in the standard versions). Also, it wasn't just Atlantis that was destroyed, it was the world as it was before the Ladder. Irem doesn't have that. The Judges were there before, and they are still here.<br /> <br /> Just to clarify, I agree with you on Pangea. I don't really get that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'd also love to divorce Tier from Compact/Conspiracy. A VALKYRIE cell should just as easily be a single fireteam that hears from their higher-ups every once in a blue moon for a Night at the Opera (Tier 1) as they are a jet-setting group of international military troubleshooters (Tier 3). Tier is essential to Hunter play and I'd like as many of the groups as possible to function at all levels. </div> </div> </div>I think that's a good idea.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-14T03:59:42-07:00","id":227738,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/224619-what-do-you-think-a-hunter-the-vigil-chronicle-book-should-have?p=227584#post227584\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I\u2019d love to see the Monsters mechanics from <b>Mortal Remains</b> incorporated into the <b>Hunter</b> Chronicle Book, up to and including its advice on how to make your own templates; I\u2019d also like to see the \u201cAntagonists\u201d section of the Chronicle Book include a sample write-up for at least one monster who doesn\u2019t fit any of the standard templates \u2014 say, the Moth Man from one of the <b>World of Darkness</b>\u2019 introductory fiction pieces.<br /> <br /> One of the things I loved about <b>Night Stalkers</b> and <b>Spirit Slayers</b> in particular,and also in <b>Witch Finders</b> to a lesser extent, is that their monster sections didn\u2019t try to mimic the basis gameline\u2019s protagonists too closely: e.g., <b>Night Stalkers</b> let you make a variety of different kinds of vampires, most of whom were substantially different from the Kindred. One of my disappointments with <b>Mortal Remains</b> was that this aspect of things tended to get lost: for instance, the chapter on Prometheans didn\u2019t read like wild speculation on the many different kinds of artificial beings that might show up in the WoD; rather, it read more like a beta test of the rules for the Promethean Chronicle book. I\u2019d like to see the Hunter Chronicle book rectify that by presenting at least starting points for alternate takes on each of the standard monster types: rather than focusing in on how to more closely mimic the inspiring gameline\u2019s protagonists, \u201cblur the lens\u201d to encourage the Storyteller to try different takes on them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Truth be told, There are roughly only three main parts to Hunter.<br /> <br /> The Motivation/Method of hunting, the Compacts and Conspiracies, and the Monsters themselves.<br /> <br /> Hunter in my opinion spends too much time focused on C&amp;C. While this good in drama and introducing other themes but still lacks on giving focus on why people hunt. Sure you have duty, and holy blessed homicide, and all that jazz but the reason for the Vigil is personal and I feel the mechanics as written don't reflect that.<br /> <br /> As for the monsters. Just give us a book of Dread Powers, some example monsters and the game is good to go. That's the easiest fix when it comes to Hunter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-14T04:49:52-07:00","id":227753,"title":"","content":"Motivation and Method: Method is covered by Tactics and Endowments (Conviction and Edges \u2014 not the HtR things; the ones I suggested a few posts back \u2014 would fit here, too, if the Chronicle book includes them); Motivation should be covered, IMHO, by Aspiration-like traits designed to generate Practical Experience.<br /> <br /> Monsters need a bit more than just Dread Powers, though not <i>much</i> more; as I said, I like the way <b>Mortal Remains</b> handles them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 08-14-2014, 08:37 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-14T05:17:23-07:00","id":227758,"title":"","content":"I think Hunter already has a Chronicle book...Though Mortal Remains isn't exactly B&amp;S it does do the basics.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-14T05:41:47-07:00","id":227807,"title":"","content":"What <b>Mortal Remains</b> does is more along the lines of the various \u201cstopgap measures\u201d posts on the forums; writers from the original <b>Hunter: the Vigil</b> have stated that they\u2019d like to do an actual update for <b>Hunter</b> akin to <b>Blood and Smoke</b>, not just a rules patch.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-14T10:53:29-07:00","id":228211,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/224619-what-do-you-think-a-hunter-the-vigil-chronicle-book-should-have?p=227716#post227716\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's the basic foundational ideology of the Diamond orders. It's their myth of a golden age when everything was better, however they choose to define 'better'.</div> </div> </div> </div> Well now we've gone from talking about what Atlantis/Irem were like, to talking about what their heirs think of them.<br /> <br /> While it's true that there's a lot more explicit evils in Irem; Mummies also have bad memories and lots of cultish stuff going on, and a massive difference in values from modern people - so they quite easily could think of Irem as a paradise.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile the Free Council don't think too highly of Atlantis, and it most probably wasn't actually a paradise.<br /> <br /> In short, both nations are complex and with a bit of justification you could use either as the counterpart for a Paradise Lost theme. Pangaia on the other hand, doesn't really work for the AKD.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/224619-what-do-you-think-a-hunter-the-vigil-chronicle-book-should-have?p=227716#post227716\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No one intended to destroy Atlantis as well. Also, it wasn't just Atlantis that was destroyed, it was the world as it was before the Ladder. Irem doesn't have that. The Judges were there before, and they are still here.'</div> </div> </div> </div> While Irem not destroying an entire reality is a fair point - I don't think it's that important thematically. As for Atlantis, given that it was a crowning symobl of humanity's potential, I think the Exarchs did want it gone. <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shock</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/224619-what-do-you-think-a-hunter-the-vigil-chronicle-book-should-have?p=227738#post227738\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hunter in my opinion spends too much time focused on C&amp;C. While this good in drama and introducing other themes but still lacks on giving focus on why people hunt. Sure you have duty, and holy blessed homicide, and all that jazz but the reason for the Vigil is personal and I feel the mechanics as written don't reflect that.</div> </div> </div> </div> How would you make mechanics to support that?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/224619-what-do-you-think-a-hunter-the-vigil-chronicle-book-should-have?p=227388#post227388\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd also love to divorce Tier from Compact/Conspiracy. A VALKYRIE cell should just as easily be a single fireteam that hears from their higher-ups every once in a blue moon for a Night at the Opera (Tier 1) as they are a jet-setting group of international military troubleshooters (Tier 3). Tier is essential to Hunter play and I'd like as many of the groups as possible to function at all levels.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't really have any objection to support for Tier 1 TF:V, heck it's already there. I just wish they'd also add support for Tier 3 TF:V.<br /> <br /> That said, I would hope that the Tier 1 support would give better reasons for you being Tier 1 than &quot;Conspiracy brass screw over the little guys because WoD&quot;.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/224619-what-do-you-think-a-hunter-the-vigil-chronicle-book-should-have?p=227584#post227584\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I\u2019d also like to see the \u201cAntagonists\u201d section of the Chronicle Book include a sample write-up for at least one monster who doesn\u2019t fit any of the standard templates</div> </div> </div> </div> You mean Slashers? I kid <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/224619-what-do-you-think-a-hunter-the-vigil-chronicle-book-should-have?p=227584#post227584\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One of the things I loved about <b>Night Stalkers</b> and <b>Spirit Slayers</b> in particular,and also in <b>Witch Finders</b> to a lesser extent, is that their monster sections didn\u2019t try to mimic the basis gameline\u2019s protagonists too closely: e.g., <b>Night Stalkers</b> let you make a variety of different kinds of vampires, most of whom were substantially different from the Kindred.</div> </div> </div> </div> I kind of wish we did a little more on that in Dream Catchers...<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-14T18:11:14-07:00","id":228610,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/224619-what-do-you-think-a-hunter-the-vigil-chronicle-book-should-have?p=227807#post227807\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What <b>Mortal Remains</b> does is more along the lines of the various \u201cstopgap measures\u201d posts on the forums; writers from the original <b>Hunter: the Vigil</b> have stated that they\u2019d like to do an actual update for <b>Hunter</b> akin to <b>Blood and Smoke</b>, not just a rules patch.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank goodness!<br /> I love Mortal Remains but it the update Appendix feels like a stopgap and the idea that the people behind it want to give it a bigger treatment fills me with joy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-14T19:00:31-07:00","id":228634,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/224619-what-do-you-think-a-hunter-the-vigil-chronicle-book-should-have?p=228211#post228211\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Well now we've gone from talking about what Atlantis/Irem were like, to talking about what their heirs think of them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, of course. What they were \u201creally like\u201d is unimportant; what their heirs think of them is vital. (I exaggerate\u2026 slightly.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/224619-what-do-you-think-a-hunter-the-vigil-chronicle-book-should-have?p=228211#post228211\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While it's true that there's a lot more explicit evils in Irem; Mummies also have bad memories and lots of cultish stuff going on, and a massive difference in values from modern people - so they quite easily could think of Irem as a paradise.</div> </div> </div> </div>But in general, they don\u2019t. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/224619-what-do-you-think-a-hunter-the-vigil-chronicle-book-should-have?p=228211#post228211\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Meanwhile the Free Council don't think too highly of Atlantis, and it most probably wasn't actually a paradise.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Libertines don\u2019t think highly of Atlantis, but neither do they think poorly of Atlantis; in general, they don\u2019t think about Atlantis at all. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/224619-what-do-you-think-a-hunter-the-vigil-chronicle-book-should-have?p=228211#post228211\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While Irem not destroying an entire reality is a fair point - I don't think it's that important thematically. As for Atlantis, given that it was a crowning symobl of humanity's potential, I think the Exarchs did want it gone.</div> </div> </div> </div>I\u2019m sure they do. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/224619-what-do-you-think-a-hunter-the-vigil-chronicle-book-should-have?p=228211#post228211\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How would you make mechanics to support that?</div> </div> </div> </div>Aspirations for Practical Experience?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/224619-what-do-you-think-a-hunter-the-vigil-chronicle-book-should-have?p=228211#post228211\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't really have any objection to support for Tier 1 TF:V, heck it's already there. I just wish they'd also add support for Tier 3 TF:V.<br /> <br /> That said, I would hope that the Tier 1 support would give better reasons for you being Tier 1 than &quot;Conspiracy brass screw over the little guys because WoD&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Bear in mind that the poster was using \u201cTier 3\u201d in the sense that I had outlined. In that sense, TFV has Tier 3 locked up, but not Tier 1. Would I like to see TFV offer more support for TFV as a large, well-funded and well-organized paramilitary organization? Sure, that would be nice. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/224619-what-do-you-think-a-hunter-the-vigil-chronicle-book-should-have?p=228211#post228211\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You mean Slashers? I kid <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Taking it seriously though: Slashers are a funhouse mirror of hunters themselves. I\u2019m talking about options that don\u2019t parallel <i>any</i> of the published gamelines. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/224619-what-do-you-think-a-hunter-the-vigil-chronicle-book-should-have?p=228211#post228211\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I kind of wish we did a little more on that in Dream Catchers...</div> </div> </div> </div>Likewise.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 08-14-2014, 10:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-14T22:24:07-07:00","id":228791,"title":"","content":"A big book-where chapter one is monster descriptions from history, folklore, fiction writing, tv, movies...etc. chapter two-all the monster powers you can think of. Chapter 3-&quot;merits and flaws&quot; for monsters. By which I mean ways to customize a vampire to fit buffy, normal kindred, bram stokers, lestat. Basically racial add on buffs and negatives to make 3-4 not just different types of kindred, but breeds period. Genetic vamp, cursed by god vamp, chemically made vamp...and repeat for each splat. Chapter 4-ideas for completely off the wall beasties. Chapter 5-...profit?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=392\" data-tempid=\"temp_392_1519878565794_106\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3676-manbearpig","name":"ManBearPig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3676_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"148"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-15T00:24:27-07:00","id":228855,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/224619-what-do-you-think-a-hunter-the-vigil-chronicle-book-should-have?p=228634#post228634\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But in general, they don\u2019t.</div> </div> </div> </div> I get the impression that's because the books are weighted towards seeking Apothoseis rather than the average mummy. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/224619-what-do-you-think-a-hunter-the-vigil-chronicle-book-should-have?p=228634#post228634\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Libertines don\u2019t think highly of Atlantis, but neither do they think poorly of Atlantis; in general, they don\u2019t think about Atlantis at all.</div> </div> </div> </div> But when other Mage's bring it up (which is often) they generally disbelieve in the idea that Atlantis was a utopia.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/224619-what-do-you-think-a-hunter-the-vigil-chronicle-book-should-have?p=228634#post228634\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Aspirations for Practical Experience?</div> </div> </div> </div> It could be a start, but it's not enough to be the whole picture.<br /> <br /> At the very least Motivation would have to tie into the code somehow; and you'd need rules for it to develop in play. What happens if your motivation is to kill a particular monster and you pull it off? Go home, get some sleep, and go back to regular life (it's an option?) - how do you keep the game going? Or what if you want revenge on Werewolves and you discover proof that acually it was a Vampire with Protean who killed your family?<br /> <br /> I'd also think it should tie into your Code; you should have some mechanical inticement to make your Code an extension of your Motivation. If you want revenge against Werewolves than a code against Vampires or all monsters is a bit harder. I think we can trust people not to munchkin their way to hating all monsters.<br /> <br /> You could also tie it into C&amp;Cs; with each group having a motivation. And while you get internal advantages for matching your Code to your personal Motivation; you get external bonuses relating to your CorC if your Motivation matches theirs. Though that's probably over complicated and belongs as an optional rule in Cults (where I got it from).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/224619-what-do-you-think-a-hunter-the-vigil-chronicle-book-should-have?p=228634#post228634\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Bear in mind that the poster was using \u201cTier 3\u201d</div> </div> </div> </div> I thought he meant Tier as in size and &quot;organised-ness&quot; of the organisation - but atamajakki is right here; we can just ask what he meant <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/224619-what-do-you-think-a-hunter-the-vigil-chronicle-book-should-have?p=228634#post228634\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Taking it seriously though: Slashers are a funhouse mirror of hunters themselves. I\u2019m talking about options that don\u2019t parallel <i>any</i> of the published gamelines.</div> </div> </div> </div> I was going to propose David Ike style lizard conspiracy people - because Conspiracies, but that could be a funhouse mirror of Hunters as well. How about &quot;pollution monsters&quot;; mutants created by chemical dumping, radiation, etc. Something regular humanity created?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/224619-what-do-you-think-a-hunter-the-vigil-chronicle-book-should-have?p=228634#post228634\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Likewise.</div> </div> </div> </div>Want to work on it?<br /> <br /> Speaking of which, where is flyboy?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-15T01:07:30-07:00","id":228873,"title":"","content":"Pollution monsters: riff off of Nuclear Prometheans and Pandorans, but caused by a wider variety of pollutants than just nuclear radiation. <br /> <br /> Variations on the themes of the gameline monsters covers a lot of ground; but there\u2019s still room for Outsiders.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-15T11:49:34-07:00","id":229347,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> While it's true that there's a lot more explicit evils in Irem; Mummies also have bad memories and lots of cultish stuff going on, and a massive difference in values from modern people - so they quite easily could think of Irem as a paradise. </div> </div> </div>You know what? You're right. That's actually a really good point I hadn't considered. A lot of Mummies probably do think of Irem as a kind of lost paradise and would tell their cultists as such.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-15T17:49:37-07:00","id":229776,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/224619-what-do-you-think-a-hunter-the-vigil-chronicle-book-should-have?p=229347#post229347\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You know what? You're right. That's actually a really good point I hadn't considered. A lot of Mummies probably do think of Irem as a kind of lost paradise and would tell their cultists as such.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not so much as a paradise as much as &quot;Our society was the first and the best working. We didn't have any that democracy crap nor that silly 'human rights' ideas that you guys keep having. We pulled ourselves up by our bootstraps, beat anyone who wasn't in our society over the head, and anyone who didn't prove his worth was gutted to appease the gods.&quot; <br /> <br /> Not paradise but most certainly some rose colored glasses stuff going on there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-16T07:13:48-07:00","id":230196,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Mighty Grendel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/224619-what-do-you-think-a-hunter-the-vigil-chronicle-book-should-have?p=227023#post227023\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm very much in favor of the Tier ideas expressed above and would, in fact, be in favor of going just a bit further. Instead of Tiers merely representing the scope of select organizations, I think it'd be neat if the book contained rules for modifying the existing compacts and conspiracies to fit that level of scope.<br /> <br /> For example: VASCU. Tier 1 &quot;The Basement&quot; (VASCU consists of a Cell of FBI Hunters working X-files like cases) &gt;&gt; Tier 2 VASCU as written &gt;&gt; Tier 3 &quot;The Vanguard&quot; (VASCU as an international Interpol-like organization given their mandate by the UN, maybe spun off even more from the Society of the Twelve Keys).</div> </div> </div> </div>This works better for some groups than others, but I <i>really</i> like it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/224619-what-do-you-think-a-hunter-the-vigil-chronicle-book-should-have?p=227343#post227343\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Technically yes, but metaphorically I'd say no. They're extra-judicial death squads commanded by unknown people (for the characters at least) for unknown purposes. TFV asks the question of whether you're actually fighting against the conspiracies that choke the WoD or have you simply joined one of those conspiracies.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which makes it even more fitting that they're the group that's canonically subverted. It's also one of the groups where &quot;monster hunter&quot; is an actual profession - it's a different way of stepping out of the mundane world, but you've still done so.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-16T17:28:54-07:00","id":230720,"title":"","content":"I wouldn\u2019t mind a mechanic to \u201croll back\u201d the Code, with immersing yourself in your Profession being one way to reinforce the effort.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-16T18:11:58-07:00","id":230742,"title":"","content":"So I thought about going and refuting Raven's counter AKD/Mages/Werewolves things, then noticed I had four likes and a lot of people indulging my argument and none for him, so I think that speaks as much as I want to bother saying.<br /> <br /> I want a more compelling Chapter 1.(Which will probably be Chapter 2 in second edition)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-17T19:17:57-07:00","id":232196,"title":"","content":"If time and funds allow, I hope that they get Chuck Wendig back to develop Vigil 2e.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage the Awakening 2e Communal Homebrew Threads:<br /> - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/966394-perils-of-the-path-post-your-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Perils of the Path</a> - Other homebrew threads linked in the OP!<br /> <br /> Join us at the unofficial IRC channels on.irc.sorcery.net at #exalted and now #theonyxpath!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/451-kirby-jerusalem","name":"Kirby Jerusalem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar451_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T10:37:14-07:00","id":233013,"title":"","content":"I would like to see a mechanic for building your own Compact/Conspiracy. As in, players rack up experience, man-power and finance throughout the game, and the lonely Hunter cell slowly developes into something much bigger and grander even as its members gains increasingly more contacts and allies through their work and Professions.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1958-krobeles","name":"Krobeles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1958_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T12:05:50-07:00","id":233115,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Krobeles</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/224619-what-do-you-think-a-hunter-the-vigil-chronicle-book-should-have?p=233013#post233013\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would like to see a mechanic for building your own Compact/Conspiracy. As in, players rack up experience, man-power and finance throughout the game, and the lonely Hunter cell slowly developes into something much bigger and grander even as its members gains increasingly more contacts and allies through their work and Professions.</div> </div> </div> </div>This would be very, very awesome.<br /> <br /> In addition, I think I'd like Tactics to be reworked as they're the other major advantage Hunters use alongside Endowments, but they never seem to get any love? Or at the least I tend not to see them being discussed as readily as Endowments, which is kinda understandable given how working as a team isn't quite as flashy as praying on some armor. Tilts and Conditions can help codify what Tactics can do and how well they do them.<br /> <br /> And this is a thought I had just now that may or may not be practical, but maybe Hunters could also use the Reversal Points idea from Imperial Mysteries? Archmages have them because they're individually powerful entities with tons of &quot;friends&quot;, connections, and boatloads of attribute dots, so the idea that they can set up some crazy gambits is to be expected. While Tier 2 and 3 organizations don't have the sheer supernatural weight of a single Archmage, they are still well-connected orginizations with tons of &quot;friends&quot;, connections, and collectively speaking a boatload of attribute dots. These &quot;revisions&quot; would take some sort of setup though, since, well, Conspiracies have red tape that the PCs need to cut or be burned with. Maybe in order to use a Reversal Point, a condition must be met for some period of time before the points can be &quot;called in&quot; to be used, representing the set up and the eventual payoff. Break the condition though, and the point is lost.<br /> <br /> I'll admit, this might not be the best idea for Hunter for reasons that other posters will come up with, so I guess in the end what really, really want in a theoretical 2nd Edition Hunter is some really new and awesome stuff that makes me go &quot;holy fuck, Hunters own!&quot;<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/671-the-lone-gunman","name":"The Lone Gunman","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T12:11:11-07:00","id":233124,"title":"","content":"Actually reversal points for Hunter is a really great idea!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-20T05:22:16-07:00","id":235321,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Dataweaver:</b> OTOH, I also don\u2019t think that \u201ctier\u201d should be used as a synonym for \u201ccells, compacts, or conspiracies\u201d. Rather, Tiers should be described in terms of intended play-style ... <i>Tier One</i> is for those Storytellers who like the notion that hunters are no different from regular mortals ... <i>Tier Two</i> assumes that the protagonists are something special, though not supernatural ... <i>Tier Three</i> assumes that the lines between mortal and monster have been blurred, and that hunters have reason to question which side of that line they stand on. </div> </div> </div>I mostly agree with this for Tiers 1 and 3; for Tier 2, I'd refine it a bity to include the Vigil having developed to the point where there's a definite philosophy of what the supernatural and the Vigil <i>mean</i> something more than monsters bad/protect innocent) - so Tier 1 has you seeing and reacting to the supernatural world, Tier 2 has you taking a few steps into it, and Tier 3 has you in danger of becoming part of it (Tier 4 in this model would presumably be like playing a rogue ghoul or a Banisher <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />). Under this model, Advanced Armoury would make sense for Tier 2, since it's essentially high tech. I'd argue that Relics can as well - despite the proprietary interest of AkD, they're gizmos everyone can use and no one can make, which makes them particularly emblematic of the idea that the supernatural world is something &quot;beyond.&quot; On the other hand, Benedictions, Castigation, Elixirs (for which you have to develop your bodily immunities), and Thaumotech would all be Tier 3. The psychic powers of VASCU could be either one, depending on how you view the implications of the other planes they sometimes access (though the Wintergreen Process is certainly a Tier 3 deal). I wouldn't mind a general &quot;Occulstim&quot; Endowment, containing of ritual magics that you can lens onto any group you think would be more atmospheric with them (the Loyalists of Thule and Maiden's Blood Sisterhood are both rumoured to have magicians of some stripe).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-20T05:24:01-07:00","id":235327,"title":"","content":"Does anyone else have trouble getting this site to accept line breaks in posts?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-20T10:03:21-07:00","id":235520,"title":"","content":"Tiers should be<br /> <br /> 1) The hunters have just scratched at the surface of the World of Darkness, they are disorganized &amp; unequipped to deal with the darkness<br /> <br /> 2) The hunters have passed through the fire &amp; flames &amp; came out stronger, they know what they are dealing with now &amp; the resources to combat it<br /> <br /> 3) The hunters have the seen strings being pulled behind the world &amp; now are pulling a few themselves, their territory is no longer a small town or neighborhood. They have manpower, resources &amp; clout to effect real change<br /> <br /> This should be separate from Endowments. I can see a lot of different imaginings on how someone who isn't in a Conspiracy could have Endowments, though I fully recommend that there should be at least one Conspiracy for each Endowments or maybe two<br /> <br /> Benedictions - A country priest finds that the holy rites he performs regularly suddenly start to really work, &amp; though he may not understand his place in his divine plan, he knows that he must answer the Call<br /> Castigation - This is literally about your bloodline, not your membership in a super special club.<br /> Thaumaturgy - A desperate vet, with heart complications, figures that if that man-wolf thing he shot could recover from the injury why not try cutting the regenerating organs &amp; see if they don't wear out; A group of hobos that graft parts from the monsters that would prey on them, so they can better survive the mean streets<br /> Elixirs - A high school teacher learns about the occult &amp; starts doing some alchemy, a drug lord's top producer finds a way to enhance the drug lord's enforcers<br /> etc.<br /> <br /> &amp; I'd like to see support for every level of play. I like to play Tier 1-2 where the PC's are just average joes, thrust into the world, but I like them to have options &amp; interesting things, like Castigation or Benediction","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2266,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2266-aermas","user":"Aermas","date":". 08-20-2014, 01:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2266-aermas","name":"Aermas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2266_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"128"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-20T11:20:01-07:00","id":235596,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SunlessNick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/224619-what-do-you-think-a-hunter-the-vigil-chronicle-book-should-have?p=235327#post235327\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does anyone else have trouble getting this site to accept line breaks in posts?</div> </div> </div> </div>Only when I copy and paste from google docs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-28T09:11:22-07:00","id":243189,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kirby Jerusalem</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/224619-what-do-you-think-a-hunter-the-vigil-chronicle-book-should-have?p=232196#post232196\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If time and funds allow, I hope that they get Chuck Wendig back to develop Vigil 2e.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Not too likely. Did you know one of his novel series just got picked up by the Starz network? He's doing very well right now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-05T08:26:08-07:00","id":272949,"title":"","content":"Hooray!<br /> <br /> I mean,shame we won't get him again? But I'm glad things are going really well for him.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-08T01:10:56-07:00","id":275247,"title":"","content":"Break the association between SIZE and &quot;Tier 3 Endowments&quot; upfront. Some &quot;conspiracies&quot; that wield supernatural Endowments are going to be small-insular mystery cults. Some &quot;compacts&quot; that don't may be international networks of cells.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-13T23:52:59-07:00","id":280647,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/alchemical-recipes/\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://theonyxpath.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/11/OPP-Metal.png\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/alchemical-recipes/\" target=\"_blank\"> Alchemical Recipes [Promethean: The Created] &ndash; Onyx Path Publishing </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/alchemical-recipes/\" target=\"_blank\"> http://theonyxpath.com/alchemical-recipes/ </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> &gt; I wanted to do a Compact started by Mary Shelley (or maybe her sister) for Mortal Remains, but I ran out of space.<br /> Does anyone know something about that Compact? Maybe some open development information?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4077-rbk","name":"RBK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-15T17:52:54-07:00","id":282963,"title":"","content":"I agree that the new chronicle book aught to have separated tiers (local, regional, global, cosmic) from organization scale (cell, compact, conspiracy).<br /> <br /> Also perhaps like a vampire joining a covenant some groups aught to get group specific powers, but that there aught to be powers available for all hunters too (like disciplines), or maybe all endowments aught to be allowed, they just aught to be more expensive for &quot;out of group&quot;. Things like the ability to summon and banish &quot;demons&quot; (not necessarily DtD)(as someone put, like in supernatural). Maybe the &quot;ritual magic&quot; from witch finders could be something hunters could get too (fits slippery slope theme). More advanced armory things (liquid sunlight) (and the ability to create them), or hunter specific relics (colt's gun in the show supernatural, which would have been &quot;advanced armory&quot; in colt's time).<br /> <br /> More focus on tactics and team work. Some people have mentioned larger group ops, and I think that'd be a good idea.<br /> <br /> I also like the idea of hunters getting a Potency trait themselves (purchased like it), which can also be used for resistance. This is not an immunity, you just perhaps get a higher than normal rating against things like Lunacy, Disquiet, etc. Easily explained as resistance building, awareness, lack of disbelief.<br /> <br /> It's worth noting that I don't want hunters to become more inhuman, I just want to give them more of an edge. Some of which might be rules basically geared towards using the supernatural against the supernatural.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.pinterest.com/xenoterracide/chrod-inspirations/\" target=\"_blank\">Graphic Inspirational Photos for Chronicles of Darkness on Pinterest</a> <br /> <a href=\"https://chroniclesofdarkness.slack.com\" target=\"_blank\">Chronicles of Darkness Slack</a> (PM Me with Email for an Invite, then invite your friends)","edited":{"userid":4046,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4046-xenoterracide","user":"xenoterracide","date":". 10-15-2014, 09:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4046-xenoterracide","name":"xenoterracide","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"563"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-20T18:42:48-07:00","id":288126,"title":"","content":"generally my ideas seemed to have been covered already :P <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/224619-what-do-you-think-a-hunter-the-vigil-chronicle-book-should-have?p=225259#post225259\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm going to agree that Compacts and Conspiracies could use some work in a hypothetical Hunter chronicle. There should be a more clear distinction between what sets apart the two categories of organizations - the latter having access to full-sized Endowments isn't a very compelling or consistent reason, I think. Other than that, fully integrating the Code with Integrity as opposed to Morality is an obvious feature.<br /> <br /> Other than that, some new Merits might be nice, since Professional Training is no longer a &quot;Hunter thing&quot;. New Endowments, too. A lot of room for non-critical but fun content.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think new merits/endowments are key, a hunter gaining access to crazier stuff as they become more powerful, leading to questions about whether they are different from the monsters seems like a really fun thing to grapple with.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Didn't anyone ever tell you not to bring claws to a gun fight?</span></b><br /><br />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3786-leicsfox","name":"LeicsFox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3786_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"42"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-21T06:10:13-07:00","id":288477,"title":"","content":"In my headcanon, the reason why only conspiracies have endowments is basically just darwinism. Hunters with endowments would logically have an easier time recruiting (because really which sounds like a more compelling offer? &quot;Join us and fight monsters&quot; or &quot;Join us and fight monsters and gain supernatural powers/fantastic toys/whatever.&quot;) and thanks to those endowments the hunters they recruit last longer meaning that turnover is less of an issue, allowing the potential conspiracy to grow in manpower.<br /> <br /> The johnson family cult would be an example of such a proto-conspiracy, they have a supernatural advantage but they aren't a conspiracy...yet, ditto the Promethean Brotherhood who have the beginning of an endowment along with the numbers to quickly become a full blown conspiracy. <br /> <br /> And of course compacts and conspiracies has minor endowments for compacts, which I would hope would be retained in mind for hunter second ed. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-29T09:33:57-07:00","id":295930,"title":"","content":"I'd like to see a focus in the antagonist section for more unique, urban legend style monsters or even just supernatural phenomena. Maybe they don't focus so much on understanding and solving it as Mages do, but learning enough about it to contain it or protect normal people from it should be a part of any Vigil. To steal a phrase; Secure, Contain, Protect.<br /> <br /> In fact, I might even go so far as to throw in some of the guidelines you find in places for posting creepypasta as helpful in creating odd stuff for hunters to encounter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/759-willr","name":"WillR","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar759_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-09T02:12:35-08:00","id":307275,"title":"","content":"I agree that Endowments should be available at any level of Hunter Tier. For me, the tier system would more indicate the resources and activity of Hunter groups. Lower-tier groups would have more freedom, but less impressive resources. Conspiracies and such would be involved in much more politics and side activities, but they would also have more powerful endowments/equipment, as well support.<br /> <br /> I agree with The King's Raven about the <b>Aegis Kai Doru</b> having a closer relationship with mummies, maybe even elevating them to the role of primary enemy for the conspiracy. I disagree with them having an Illuminati feel, because to me that would indicate a focus on gaining political power, which I don't think the <b>Aegis Kai Doru</b> is really interested in.<br /> <br /> A number of people have thought up a Judaism-aligned conspiracy which I honestly think might not be a bad idea (I've liked both The King's Raven's conspiracy; <b>Hakollel shel Hamerkava</b>, and LostLight's conspiracy; <b>Raziel LTD</b>\u200b).<br /> <br /> For the <b>Lucifuge</b>, I think there should be an expansion on the struggle of fighting one's inner darkness. They're children of SATAN\u2026 I think that there might be some darkness there. I think that would be a great angle for the Conspiracy--half the time they are fighting creatures of darkness while utilizing dark powers strait from Hell, the other half is spent fighting their own personal demons; that little voice in the back of their head telling them to torment and manipulate the puny humans.<br /> <br /> The <b>Ascending Ones</b> I think should be built up a bit. They have a very DC Comics League of Assassins-vibe to me, and I think it might serve to expand in that direction. A Muslim/Egyptian-based hunter trained in martial arts and meditative techniques, utilizing not only those potent alchemical potions to empower themselves, but also alchemically-poisoned weapons like swords and arrows.<br /> <br /> I think it also might be a very appealing idea to expand <b>The Loyalists of Thule</b> into a mad-science conspiracy. I mean, it wasn't really any secret that the Nazi scientists were experimenting with the supernatural, so it might make sense that after the fall of Nazi Germany the Occult Science group went underground and now prowl the night, as much mad-scientists as they ever were. In their studies they utilize such devices as radios powered by the heads of dead Psychics and other bizarre occult devices.<br /> <br /> For <b>Task Force: VALKYRIE</b>, some part of me thinks that Advanced Armory isn't quite enough. To me, <b>TF: V</b> is one of the few Conspiracies which might be open to using supernatural creatures in their hunt for monsters. Though they may not employ such tricky creatures as vampires and such, I could definitely see them utilizing psychics, sin-eaters, and even changelings as agents in the field (some monsters love their country, after all). Or, if not as actual operatives then perhaps as informants and spies.<br /> <br /> As for the <b>Malleus Maleficarum</b>\u2026I think Benedictions could be a bit more nuanced\u2026like divided between prayers and blessed items (I always found it odd that though the <b>Aegis Kai Doru</b> used Catholic relics, the <b>MM</b> didn't). First you might have the regular benedictions or specialized prayers involving such things as ritualized fasting, self-flagellation, etc.. which would help channel lesser blessings and saintly might. Then you might have access to a number of very powerful, yet unstable, holy items strait from the Vatican's vaults--ancient reliquaries, the remains of various unofficial saints, nails used to crucify martyrs, etc.--to use as banes and weapons.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1868,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1868-hellovg","user":"hellovg","date":". 11-09-2014, 05:56 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1868-hellovg","name":"hellovg","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"165"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-09T03:10:01-08:00","id":307288,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hellovg</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/224619-what-do-you-think-a-hunter-the-vigil-chronicle-book-should-have?p=307275#post307275\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I agree with The King's Raven about the <b>Aegis Kai Doru</b> having a closer relationship with mummies, maybe even elevating them to the role of primary enemy for the conspiracy. I disagree with them having an Illuminati feel, because to me that would indicate a focus on gaining political power, which I don't think the <b>Aegis Kai Doru</b> is really interested in.</div> </div> </div> </div>I actaully agree that it's not something in the current write up; rather it's something I think will fill a gap in the current write up. All the organisations have something that they hunt, but also something that they are. Something to stand for, something to stand against. I think you need both.<br /> <br /> TF:V is American government, it hunts threats to America.<br /> <br /> The MM are Catholics, they hunt vampires, witches, demons and other monsters in that order.<br /> <br /> The AKD only has that second one. They hunt Relics, Witches and Werewolves. But what are they?<br /> <br /> You can sort of see the beginnings of an answer, they're an ancient conspiracy who decsend from a lost utopia; but unlike &quot;catholic church&quot; where two words gives you all the information you need, it's left vague and undefined. So I want to give them more definition, I don't want to define and lock down the truth of their origin (a list of options is fine) but I do want to define and lock down their present day beliefs. Give them a reason to want those relics beyond &quot;they're our right dammit!&quot;<br /> <br /> The illuminati angle provides that. Once you say illumanti storytellers have a wealth of ideas to mine and create their day to day activites from. Secret meetings, mason lodges, and of course their long term plan. There needs to be at least one Conspiracy who's proactive, who has a goal and works towards it rather than just reacting to monsters.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hellovg</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/224619-what-do-you-think-a-hunter-the-vigil-chronicle-book-should-have?p=307275#post307275\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A number of people have thought up a Judaism-aligned conspiracy, which I honestly think might not be a bad idea. The three branches of Abrahamic faith are big enough and zealous enough to have monster-slaying groups in them.</div> </div> </div> </div> Thanks you <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> HsH probably straddles the line between Compact and Conspiracy if you don't go by Endowments. Their Endowment is crazy powerful and they have a lot of non-Endowment magic (Kaballaists are a form of Second Sight's Thamaturges, though I prefer to give them a major power bump along the lines of the Sons of Phobos from Bllood Sorcery) relative to their size. I might just be ignorant, but I can't think of any magical practition in Christianity that's accepted like Kaballa is.<br /> <br /> But apart from their Enowment they don't really have much. They're smaller than most Conspiracies (Lucifuge excepted, of course) and have little organisation. It's lots of rabbis each with their own local sphere of inlfuence, though they probably have some clout in America's (in)famous Jewish lobby and a few politicians in the Knesset - which due to the way Israeli politics works is actually a fair bit of power. Just not nearly as much as the Catholic Church's or the Men in Black's.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hellovg</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/224619-what-do-you-think-a-hunter-the-vigil-chronicle-book-should-have?p=307275#post307275\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For the <b>Lucifuge</b>, I think there should be an expansion on the struggle of fighting one's inner darkness.</div> </div> </div> </div> I like it. Maybe using Castigation requires them to accept all sorts of Conditions that can either be resolved the hard way, or the quick and sinful way.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hellovg</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/224619-what-do-you-think-a-hunter-the-vigil-chronicle-book-should-have?p=307275#post307275\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The <b>Ascending Ones</b> I think should be built up a bit.</div> </div> </div> </div> I kind of think they mostly have that direction already; just with Elixirs doing the heavy lifting. I wouldn't say no to expanding it, but I'd keep the focus on Elixirs. So those meditative techniques require a drink or insence.<br /> <br /> Poisoned weapons, definately. No one's ever made a gun as quiet as a bow. Or heck, Alchemical gunpowder that doesn't make a sound would make an awesome one dot Elixir.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hellovg</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/224619-what-do-you-think-a-hunter-the-vigil-chronicle-book-should-have?p=307275#post307275\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think it also might be a very appealing idea to combine the <b>Null Mysteriis </b>and <b>The Loyalists of Thule</b> into one mad-science conspiracy.</div> </div> </div> </div> I'm not a fan. Null Mysteriis are legitimate scientists not mad scientists. I wouldn't want to loose that angle, same with the Loyalists. I don't want to give up the redemption angel.<br /> <br /> Besides, both KSI-21 (sadly only 1/3 written) and MI18 scratch my WWII mad science itch.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hellovg</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/224619-what-do-you-think-a-hunter-the-vigil-chronicle-book-should-have?p=307275#post307275\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For <b>Task Force: VALKYRIE</b>, some part of me thinks that Advanced Armory isn't quite enough.</div> </div> </div> </div> While the idea of Conspiracies employing monsters makes sense, I'd rather have a sidebar saying that TF:V and Cheiron both do it it's recomended to downplay that angle for thematic reasons.<br /> <br /> I'd much rather expand TF:V with Airstrikes, Tanks, and a sidebar on just what they can get away with. Like walking into a Vampire's bank, flashing an ID badge, and walking out with all the hard drives.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hellovg</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/224619-what-do-you-think-a-hunter-the-vigil-chronicle-book-should-have?p=307275#post307275\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for the <b>Malleus Maleficarum</b>\u2026Honestly, I think they should play up how scary this group of hunters can be, almost like the Iscariot Organization from the <i>Hellsing</i> manga/anime. Whether it be a vampire, mage, mummy, or whatever else, if the <b>MM </b>has its sights set on you, then you know you're in a world of SHIT.</div> </div> </div> </div> I actually think this about every last Conspiracy. If TF:V really wants you dead they carpet bomb you. If the AKD really really wants you dead they give one guy the Spear of Lugh (power: win <u>any</u> battle)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hellovg</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/224619-what-do-you-think-a-hunter-the-vigil-chronicle-book-should-have?p=307275#post307275\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(I always found it odd that though the <b>Aegis Kai Doru</b> used Catholic relics, the <b>MM</b> didn't)</div> </div> </div> </div> My view: the MM has more Catholic relics than the AKD, but less than a hundreth of relics in total.<br /> <br /> So to the AKD giving a Catholic relic is no big deal, it's just one relic from the big pile. To the MM giving out any Relic is a big deal.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-09T03:44:49-08:00","id":307301,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> My view: the MM has more Catholic relics than the AKD, but less than a hundreth of relics in total.<br /> <br /> So to the AKD giving a Catholic relic is no big deal, it's just one relic from the big pile. To the MM giving out any Relic is a big deal. </div> </div> </div>I'm always under impression that some of Relics of Catholic nature in AKD's possession were acquired in dubious circumstances, and now MM bolts down every reliquary just to be sure. Basically, in my head Aegis Kai Doru are Relic stealing magpies like Blood Ravens in Dawn of War 2.<br /> <br /> Hide Yo Relics, Hide Yo Tokens, Hide Yo Fetishes, coz Aegis Kai Doru is coming for them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-10T17:33:41-08:00","id":308664,"title":"","content":"I'd like to see Cells, Compacts, and Conspiracies retain their individual flavors, but not feel like you're being &quot;nerfed&quot; by wanting to play only in a specific Tier. I like the idea of the Ashwood Abbey, but the Endowments of Task Force: Valkyrie are just too cool for words. Now, my hypothetical Ashwood Abby Hunter shouldn't be walking around with a raygun, but something I as an Ashwood Abbey member have that wouldn't make me look at a TF:V member with unrequited jealousy. You know, like that commercial that airs all the time when you watch The Walking Dead On Demand: the grizzled old veteran talking about how he's survived the zombie apocalypse so long, and one of the folk he's talking to replying &quot;And you have. . . that.&quot; And we see his awesome pimped-out zombie-killing ride. &quot;Yeah, but you have that.&quot; &quot;It's a stick.&quot; &quot;But it's a really sharp stick.&quot;<br /> <br /> Some of the ideas behind the Compacts are WAY cooler than those behind the Conspiracies, but playing a member of a Compact as opposed to a Conspiracy kinda feels like bringing a sharp stick to a pimped-out zombie-killing ride fight. And if you're not even in a Compact? Damn, I wish <i>I</i> had a sharp stick!<br /> <br /> Not necessarily saying &quot;Endowments for everybody!&quot; because some of the Compact's great flavors come from the fact that they aren't these global organizations with the resources to create/obtain all this outlandish stuff. The Union is awesome precisely because they're just the average Joes doin' what they can with what they got. They can't match the biotech know-how of Cheiron Group. But should they have their own ways of doing things that get just as good results? Absolutely!<br /> <br /> For instance, The Union's whole thing is that they're blue-collar workmen who've stumbled across the supernatural and are keeping their friends and family's safe. So utilize that background, give them cool things they can do relating to that background. Sure, they can't build the kinds of stuff that comes out of TF:V or Cheiron's R&amp;D departments, but if you put an electrical engineer, carpenter, and construction worker in the same room and tell them to come up with something to kill a vampire, they'll come up with something to kill that vampire DEAD. Similarly, Ashwood Abbey may not have access to artifacts or alchemical potions, but a bunch of bored socialites with nothing to do but think about their next big thrill are going to come up with some pretty intense ways as regards how to get it. I don't just mean Tactics. . . those are too integral to all Hunters, I feel, to use them as a &quot;separate but equal&quot; way of balancing things out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/4411-my-geist-gmc-updates\" target=\"_blank\">My Geist GMC Updates</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/4348-my-infinite-macabre-goodies\" target=\"_blank\">My Infinite Macabre Goodies</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/4372-parasite-eve-the-third-birthday-chronicle\" target=\"_blank\">Parasite Eve: The Third Birthday Chronicle</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/899558-shamelessly-pimping-my-book\" target=\"_blank\">Shamelessly pimping my book</a>","edited":{"userid":831,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/831-erikmodi","user":"ErikModi","date":". 11-10-2014, 08:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/831-erikmodi","name":"ErikModi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-10T17:51:19-08:00","id":308677,"title":"","content":"Like I said before: whether or not you get Endowments ought to be a separate decision from whether you\u2019re in a Conspiracy, a Compact, or an independent Cell. Sure, independent cells should lean toward \u201cordinary people in over their heads\u201d, Compacts should lean toward \u201cwell-equipped and highly competent but still fully human monster hunters\u201d, and Conspiracies should lean toward \u201cborderline-supernatural monster hunters\u201d; but just about every combination of Cell/Compact/Conspiracy and ordinary/heroic/Endowed should be supported.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-11T04:15:05-08:00","id":308931,"title":"","content":"As before, I agree. How powerful tools you get should be decoupled from the level of organization you operate on. They should be related, but not inextricably tied together.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/186-morty","name":"Morty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar186_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-11T09:53:08-08:00","id":309246,"title":"","content":"Thing is, I think they did a really awesome job giving the different Conspiracies flavor through their different Endowments. I love all the Conspiracies because their Endowments are so spot-on for who and what they are. Decoupling that would rob the Conspiracies of some of their unique flavor. I just want the unique flavor of the Compacts to be on an equal playing field with the unique flavor of the Conspiracies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/4411-my-geist-gmc-updates\" target=\"_blank\">My Geist GMC Updates</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/4348-my-infinite-macabre-goodies\" target=\"_blank\">My Infinite Macabre Goodies</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/4372-parasite-eve-the-third-birthday-chronicle\" target=\"_blank\">Parasite Eve: The Third Birthday Chronicle</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/899558-shamelessly-pimping-my-book\" target=\"_blank\">Shamelessly pimping my book</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/831-erikmodi","name":"ErikModi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-11T13:08:30-08:00","id":309418,"title":"","content":"I would hope that there\u2019s more to, say, Task Force Valkyrie than <i>just</i> having access to an Advanced Armoury. Heck, I could <i>easily</i> see a TFV-centered game centered more on heroic mortals who <i>don\u2019t</i> have access to borderline-supernatural technology. Likewise with the Malleus Maleficatorum: sure, Benedictions are a nice thing to have when confronting the supernatural; but they\u2019re not essential to what the Malleus Maleficatorum <i>is</i>. <br /> <br /> Admittedly, some Conspiracies are more tightly bound to their Endowments than others: is there anything to the Aegis Kai Doru if they\u2019re <i>not</i> collecting Relics? Is it reasonable to join the Lucifuge and <i>not</i> be demon-descended? This is why I\u2019m not advocating a <i>complete</i> decoupling of Endowments from Conspiracies; though I <i>would</i> like <b>Hunter 2e</b> to at least dedicate a paragraph for each Conspiracy examining how it might be used in a chronicle where the protagonists are assumed <i>not</i> to have access to superhuman powers. I suspect that this could be done by tweaking or expanding on the Conspiracies as written \u2014 for instance, the Lucifuge might play up mortal \u201cdemon-hunting\u201d teams who are trained to take down L\u2019Enfant Diabolique, with any reformed Children of the Seventh Generation playing supporting roles.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-11T14:00:26-08:00","id":309437,"title":"","content":"My view is simpler. I would allow Cells/Compacts to have full Conspiracy level endowments and I'd allow Conspiracies with Compact level Endowments, but I'd keep the current setup of one group one Endowment with exceptions mostly being consigned to fluff. I wouldn't give any of the current core six Compacts a full Endowment, but I would make Ashwood Abbey a Conspiracy and the Lucifuge a compact without changing their Endowments. As for a paragraph about playing Conspiracies without Endowments, is there even a paragraph's worth of useful advice to be had?<br /> <br /> As for Heroic Mortals, I think that rule belongs in Mirrors. Hunter is at it's core about ordinary mortals and what they can achieve united (and yes, supernatural powers <b>is</b> what ordinary mortals can achieve united). Heroic Mortals belong in mirrors, but giving explicit advice for the core Hunter orgs in Mirrors 2e is probably a good idea.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-11T14:06:00-08:00","id":309441,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/224619-what-do-you-think-a-hunter-the-vigil-chronicle-book-should-have?p=309418#post309418\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Admittedly, some Conspiracies are more tightly bound to their Endowments than others: is there anything to the Aegis Kai Doru if they\u2019re <i>not</i> collecting Relics? Is it reasonable to join the Lucifuge and <i>not</i> be demon-descended?</div> </div> </div> </div>AKD are nursing that wound for Mages and the Werewolves.<br /> <br /> Lucifuge on the other hand, I've always viewed that potential recruits could be gathered after a demonic event, not just being the offspring of a demon. Having only 666 members worldwide is very low and you got get the bulk of the support staff from somewhere.<br /> <br /> Hence why I typically have no problem including the offspring of normal people into the Lucifuge. They just won't have access to the juicy endowments (right away).<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-11T15:30:02-08:00","id":309528,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/224619-what-do-you-think-a-hunter-the-vigil-chronicle-book-should-have?p=309418#post309418\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would hope that there\u2019s more to, say, Task Force Valkyrie than <i>just</i> having access to an Advanced Armoury.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, absolutely. But their Advanced Armory is a part of who they are, and having other Hunters walking around with the exact same equipment would kind of. . . steal their <i>thunder.</i><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/224619-what-do-you-think-a-hunter-the-vigil-chronicle-book-should-have?p=309418#post309418\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Heck, I could <i>easily</i> see a TFV-centered game centered more on heroic mortals who <i>don\u2019t</i> have access to borderline-supernatural technology. Likewise with the Malleus Maleficatorum: sure, Benedictions are a nice thing to have when confronting the supernatural; but they\u2019re not essential to what the Malleus Maleficatorum [i]is</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, yeah. But all other things being equal Endowments are kind of the selling point for an individual group. If I like the fluff behind TF:V and MM equally, the reason I'll go with one and not the other is because I'd rather have an awesome Stark Industries gun than magic banishing powers, or vice versa.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/224619-what-do-you-think-a-hunter-the-vigil-chronicle-book-should-have?p=309418#post309418\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Admittedly, some Conspiracies are more tightly bound to their Endowments than others: is there anything to the Aegis Kai Doru if they\u2019re <i>not</i> collecting Relics? Is it reasonable to join the Lucifuge and <i>not</i> be demon-descended? This is why I\u2019m not advocating a <i>complete</i> decoupling of Endowments from Conspiracies;</div> </div> </div> </div>We're on the same page there.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/224619-what-do-you-think-a-hunter-the-vigil-chronicle-book-should-have?p=309418#post309418\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">though I <i>would</i> like <b>Hunter 2e</b> to at least dedicate a paragraph for each Conspiracy examining how it might be used in a chronicle where the protagonists are assumed <i>not</i> to have access to superhuman powers.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree completely. Let any &quot;Tier&quot; of Hunter have access to any &quot;Tier&quot; of power, so you can play any given group with any level of extra badass. Or more accurately, decouple the Tier system from the Cell/Compact/Conspiracy system, so that you can have Tier 1 Conspiracy members and Tier 3 Cell members.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/224619-what-do-you-think-a-hunter-the-vigil-chronicle-book-should-have?p=309418#post309418\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I suspect that this could be done by tweaking or expanding on the Conspiracies as written \u2014 for instance, the Lucifuge might play up mortal \u201cdemon-hunting\u201d teams who are trained to take down L\u2019Enfant Diabolique, with any reformed Children of the Seventh Generation playing supporting roles.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, if you rework the Tier system so it's a little more open, than any group has the option to be &quot;just guys with no idea what we're getting into&quot; or &quot;well-trained, well-equipped troops with all the tools and talent necessary to deal with anything that comes our way,&quot; and anything in between.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/4411-my-geist-gmc-updates\" target=\"_blank\">My Geist GMC Updates</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/4348-my-infinite-macabre-goodies\" target=\"_blank\">My Infinite Macabre Goodies</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/4372-parasite-eve-the-third-birthday-chronicle\" target=\"_blank\">Parasite Eve: The Third Birthday Chronicle</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/899558-shamelessly-pimping-my-book\" target=\"_blank\">Shamelessly pimping my book</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/831-erikmodi","name":"ErikModi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-11T16:15:31-08:00","id":309554,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/224619-what-do-you-think-a-hunter-the-vigil-chronicle-book-should-have?p=309437#post309437\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My view is simpler. I would allow Cells/Compacts to have full Conspiracy level endowments and I'd allow Conspiracies with Compact level Endowments, but I'd keep the current setup of one group one Endowment with exceptions mostly being consigned to fluff. I wouldn't give any of the current core six Compacts a full Endowment, but I would make Ashwood Abbey a Conspiracy and the Lucifuge a compact without changing their Endowments.</div> </div> </div> </div>No arguments there. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/224619-what-do-you-think-a-hunter-the-vigil-chronicle-book-should-have?p=309437#post309437\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for a paragraph about playing Conspiracies without Endowments, is there even a paragraph's worth of useful advice to be had?</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure. Shock just demonstrated the essence of what the Lucifuge paragraph might cover. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/224619-what-do-you-think-a-hunter-the-vigil-chronicle-book-should-have?p=309437#post309437\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for Heroic Mortals, I think that rule belongs in Mirrors. Hunter is at it's core about ordinary mortals and what they can achieve united (and yes, supernatural powers <b>is</b> what ordinary mortals can achieve united). Heroic Mortals belong in mirrors, but giving explicit advice for the core Hunter orgs in Mirrors 2e is probably a good idea.</div> </div> </div> </div>IMHO, a large part of <b>Hunter</b> <i>is</i> <b>Mirrors</b>-style content: moreso than any other WoD gameline, <b>Hunter</b> isn\u2019t based on a single, coherent metaphysics (in-game) or a single playstyle (on a meta level). In fact, the three tiers were originally conceived of as a vehicle for incorporating three very different takes on how to play hunters into one game. As I see it, it\u2019s better to make the support for different playstyles explicit. <br /> <br /> How does this relate to Heroic Mortals<sup>*</sup>? Simple: there are a lot of folks who approach <b>Hunter</b> with the idea that the protagonists are a cut above your average mortal. Risking Willpower and Practical Experience are game systems that already exist in <b>Hunter</b> that are geared toward such \u201cexceptional mortal\u201d play. Conversely, there are those who dislike even those rules being available because <i>their</i> approach to hunters is to treat them as much like ordinary people as can be managed given the assumption that they\u2019re willing to do something about the monsters in the shadows. Including a 2e version of heroic mortals in the game is a way of catering to the \u201cI want hunters to be a cut above\u201d crowd; tying them to a particular style of play so that they\u2019re only available if the Storyteller opts in to including them is a way of catering to the \u201cI want hunters to be just like everyone else\u201d crowd. <br /> <br /> And Supernatural Merits (including, but not limited to, Endowments) are for those who want to blur the line between hunter and prey. That, too, should be presented as an option that the Storyteller shouldn\u2019t feel compelled to allow. <br /> <br /> You\u2019ve laid out a compelling vision for how <b>Hunter</b> might be played; and far be it from me to tell you not to play the game that way. But by the same token, I wouldn\u2019t want the second edition to cater exclusively to just that one style of play. As I said at the start of this section, <b>Hunter</b> is the most \u201ctoolboxy\u201d (to coin a word) of the WoD gamelines; I\u2019d like to see 2e become even moreso. <br /> <br /> <hr />* Who were introduced in <b>Strange, Dead Love</b>, BTW; not <b>Mirrors</b>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 11-11-2014, 07:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-11T16:48:57-08:00","id":309580,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ErikModi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/224619-what-do-you-think-a-hunter-the-vigil-chronicle-book-should-have?p=309528#post309528\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, absolutely. But their Advanced Armory is a part of who they are, and having other Hunters walking around with the exact same equipment would kind of. . . steal their <i>thunder.</i></div> </div> </div> </div>Eh. If their identity is so wrapped up in their Advanced Armory that introducing another group that also has Advanced Armory would undermine their very reason for being, then I humbly suggest that their concept is too shallow and needs to be deepened. That said, making Advanced Armory something that <i>everyone</i> has access to would be problematic in a number of ways: at the very least, any Compact or Conspiracy that has access to Advanced Armory ought to have some sort of paramilitary or special ops angle to it: giving Advanced Armory to a Monastic Order of the Catholic Church ain\u2019t gonna fly. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ErikModi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/224619-what-do-you-think-a-hunter-the-vigil-chronicle-book-should-have?p=309528#post309528\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, yeah. But all other things being equal Endowments are kind of the selling point for an individual group. If I like the fluff behind TF:V and MM equally, the reason I'll go with one and not the other is because I'd rather have an awesome Stark Industries gun than magic banishing powers, or vice versa.</div> </div> </div> </div>True enough. But what about drawing a distinction between TFV and, say, the Los Angeles Special Crimes Unit (a hypothetical cell that\u2019s based on LA\u2019s SWAT program, which has refined its monster-hunting gear over time to the point that it\u2019s now competitive with what TFV wields)? Both get Advanced Armory; but a distinction is drawn in terms of who they answer to and how they operate. <br /> <br /> Bottom line: I find the notion of Conspiracies (or, yes, Compacts) holding absolute monopolies on their associated Endowments (as opposed to \u201cmerely\u201d being the most well known users of said Endowments) to be needlessly restrictive. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ErikModi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/224619-what-do-you-think-a-hunter-the-vigil-chronicle-book-should-have?p=309528#post309528\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I agree completely. Let any \u201cTier\u201d of Hunter have access to any \u201cTier\u201d of power, so you can play any given group with any level of extra badass. Or more accurately, decouple the Tier system from the Cell/Compact/Conspiracy system, so that you can have Tier 1 Conspiracy members and Tier 3 Cell members.<br /> <br /> Well, if you rework the Tier system so it's a little more open, than any group has the option to be \u201cjust guys with no idea what we're getting into\u201d or \u201cwell-trained, well-equipped troops with all the tools and talent necessary to deal with anything that comes our way,\u201d and anything in between.</div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-11T18:46:44-08:00","id":309726,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ErikModi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/224619-what-do-you-think-a-hunter-the-vigil-chronicle-book-should-have?p=309528#post309528\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <b>Oh, absolutely. But their Advanced Armory is a part of who they are, and having other Hunters walking around with the exact same equipment would kind of. . . steal their <i>thunder.</i></b><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Well, yeah. But all other things being equal Endowments are kind of the selling point for an individual group. I<b>f I like the fluff behind TF:V and MM equally, the reason I'll go with one and not the other is because I'd rather have an awesome Stark Industries gun than magic banishing powers, or vice versa.</b><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> We're on the same page there.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I agree completely. <b>Let any &quot;Tier&quot; of Hunter have access to any &quot;Tier&quot; of power, so you can play any given group with any level of extra badass. Or more accurately, decouple the Tier system from the Cell/Compact/Conspiracy system, so that you can have Tier 1 Conspiracy members and Tier 3 Cell members.</b><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Well, if you rework the Tier system so it's a little more open, than any group has the option to be &quot;just guys with no idea what we're getting into&quot; or &quot;well-trained, well-equipped troops with all the tools and talent necessary to deal with anything that comes our way,&quot; and anything in between.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> ^^^ This. All of this. <br /> <br /> I'm really liking some of Erik's ideas here.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-12T00:29:19-08:00","id":309922,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shock</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/224619-what-do-you-think-a-hunter-the-vigil-chronicle-book-should-have?p=309441#post309441\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">AKD are nursing that wound for Mages and the Werewolves.</div> </div> </div> </div> I don't think that really counts. Yes, you're right that it's something other than Relics but I personally draw a distinction between &quot;who they are&quot; and &quot;who they hunt&quot;. The lack of a more solid &quot;who they are&quot; for the AKD is I think a flaw.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ErikModi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/224619-what-do-you-think-a-hunter-the-vigil-chronicle-book-should-have?p=309528#post309528\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I agree completely. Let any &quot;Tier&quot; of Hunter have access to any &quot;Tier&quot; of power, so you can play any given group with any level of extra badass. Or more accurately, decouple the Tier system from the Cell/Compact/Conspiracy system, so that you can have Tier 1 Conspiracy members and Tier 3 Cell members.</div> </div> </div> </div>Personally I'd use Cell/Compact/Conspiracy as the keyword to describe the overall size, power, and influence of a group, Tier to describe how big the story is and I don't think you need a special keyword to describe how powerful the Endowments are. E.G.<br /> <br /> VASCU (Conspiracy) vs a single slasher is Tier 1. Which is why VASCU usually wins, they have researchers, support from local SWAT teams, money, and it's all going up against what's usually one guy with a chainsaw and a hockey mask.<br /> <br /> The AKD in open war with the Pentacle is Tier 3. So it's a fair fight that's likely to end with both sides hurt and withdrawing from the conflict. The Long Night in open war against the Pentacle is also Tier 3, but the Long Night will be swiftly routed (unless God steps in).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/224619-what-do-you-think-a-hunter-the-vigil-chronicle-book-should-have?p=309554#post309554\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sure. Shock just demonstrated the essence of what the Lucifuge paragraph might cover.</div> </div> </div> </div> Not really. To me the core of the Lucifuge is about the inner demon. Shock didn't describe how to capture that with pure mortals - nor do I really think the Lucifuge is the appropriate place for it. It's one specific way of looking at inner demons, (the Loyalists of Thule are another) it would be hard to make it work without the actual genetic heratage. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/224619-what-do-you-think-a-hunter-the-vigil-chronicle-book-should-have?p=309554#post309554\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">IMHO, a large part of <b>Hunter</b> <i>is</i> <b>Mirrors</b>-style content: moreso than any other WoD gameline, <b>Hunter</b> isn\u2019t based on a single, coherent metaphysics (in-game) or a single playstyle (on a meta level). In fact, the three tiers were originally conceived of as a vehicle for incorporating three very different takes on how to play hunters into one game. As I see it, it\u2019s better to make the support for different playstyles explicit.</div> </div> </div> </div> I disagree. While Hunter is even more toolbox than other nWOD games it does have some very strong central themes that run through all Tiers of play.<br /> <br /> The concept of strength in numbers for example. Even Cells get their strength from numbers and teamwork (I.E. Tactics). The idea of ignorance and paranoia is another example.<br /> <br /> I actually think this has gone too far; and that ideas suitable for Cells were inappropriately applied to Conspiracies. Ignorance is one, the idea of your Cell being alone against the dark crops up too often in Conspiracy material. That said I don't want to completely strip Hunter of it's core themes. I want to downplay exceptional individuals and play up teamwork. Heroic Mortals have rules in Mirrors that can be applied to Hunter. IMO that's the correct way to include them.<br /> <br /> (Yeah Risking Willpower does make Hunters exceptional, but it's orders of magnitude less than Heroic Mortals. Even more importantly, every hunter gets the same perks)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Eh. If their identity is so wrapped up in their Advanced Armory that introducing another group that also has Advanced Armory would undermine their very reason for being, then I humbly suggest that their concept is too shallow and needs to be deepened.</div> </div> </div> </div> I disagree. If TFV get X identity points from Advanced Armory and Y points from everything else. TFV fans still have a good justification to protect and cherish those X points even if Y &gt; X.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-12T11:31:07-08:00","id":310407,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/224619-what-do-you-think-a-hunter-the-vigil-chronicle-book-should-have?p=309580#post309580\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Eh. If their identity is so wrapped up in their Advanced Armory that introducing another group that also has Advanced Armory would undermine their very reason for being, then I humbly suggest that their concept is too shallow and needs to be deepened. That said, making Advanced Armory something that <i>everyone</i> has access to would be problematic in a number of ways: at the very least, any Compact or Conspiracy that has access to Advanced Armory ought to have some sort of paramilitary or special ops angle to it: giving Advanced Armory to a Monastic Order of the Catholic Church ain\u2019t gonna fly.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not saying that Advanced Armory is &quot;core&quot; to their identity, but it is <i>part</i> of it. You play a TF:V Hunter because A) you like bring part of a government agency hunting monsters, B) you like the Storytelling aspects of governmental bureaucracy interfering with helping people, C) you want to have a Stark Industries raygun. Letting everyone buy from Stark Industries steals part of the identity of this specific group, in the same way that everyone being able to use demon powers messes with the Lucifuge and anyone being able to graft monster parts into their bodies messes with Cheiron Group. It's not that they'll have &quot;no&quot; identity if their Endowments are available to everyone, but that part of that identity will be lost, and unless something equally interesting crops up to replace it, all of them will be damaged.<br /> <br /> Also, there isn't really a case of &quot;gameplay and story segregation&quot; in Endowments and Conspiracies. A lot of the Endowments proceed naturally from what that Conspiracy is and how it chooses to pursue the Vigil. TF:V uses pure science (at least, allegedly), Cheiron Group tries to scientifically understand mystical processes, Malleus Malificarum relies on Dark Age dogmatic ritual, the Lucifuge takes their innate curses and turns them into blessings, the Aegis Kai Doru breaks out the big guns they've been collecting for centuries, etc. Part of the great character and potential conflict between the Conspiracies comes from their different approaches to the Vigil, reflected through their Endowments. TF:V Hunters considering MM members hopelessly backward for still reading the same incantations out of ancient books, CG being all smug about their edge over TF:V because TF:V's scientists are only looking at half the picture, the MM and Lucifuge approaching the same end through two very different means. This character, I feel, would be lost were all Endowments available to all groups.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/224619-what-do-you-think-a-hunter-the-vigil-chronicle-book-should-have?p=309580#post309580\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">True enough. But what about drawing a distinction between TFV and, say, the Los Angeles Special Crimes Unit (a hypothetical cell that\u2019s based on LA\u2019s SWAT program, which has refined its monster-hunting gear over time to the point that it\u2019s now competitive with what TFV wields)? Both get Advanced Armory; but a distinction is drawn in terms of who they answer to and how they operate.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd still say that the Compact doesn't have access to the same kinds of research and development that a funded Federal agency does, but they could come up with some pretty wicked ad hoc solutions that would have their own individual character. Some items might be the same (both could easily create the sunlight flash-bangs), but instead of the Mjolnir Cannon the SWAT team perhaps weapons less overtly destructive, but more tailored to individual threats. Perhaps a weapon with different firing modes or ammo loads designed to exploit the weaknesses of different types of supernatural.<br /> <br /> Now, that's not to say that Compacts can't be &quot;sponsored&quot; by Conspiracies, kind of as &quot;seed teams&quot; from which to draw talent. In this case, a Cell or Compact could have access to a Conspiracies Endowments because that Conspiracy is funding them, but keeping them separate for some reason.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/224619-what-do-you-think-a-hunter-the-vigil-chronicle-book-should-have?p=309580#post309580\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Bottom line: I find the notion of Conspiracies (or, yes, Compacts) holding absolute monopolies on their associated Endowments (as opposed to \u201cmerely\u201d being the most well known users of said Endowments) to be needlessly restrictive.</div> </div> </div> </div>And I feel it adds character and flavor to those groups. Lucifuge with Mjolnir Cannons and MM members with demonic powers just seems off to me. I'd rather see the gameplay mechanics continue to reinforce every group's unique character and flavor, then try and handwave away how you can be an AKD member who doesn't bother hunting artifacts because he's got a raygun, or an MM member who still claims he's doing God's work while summoning demons, or a government employee who goes into dangerous situations doped to the gills on a near-fatal concoction.<br /> <br /> And what. . . no love for my Mjolnir Cannon pun? Come on, guys, I worked hard on that one!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/4411-my-geist-gmc-updates\" target=\"_blank\">My Geist GMC Updates</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/4348-my-infinite-macabre-goodies\" target=\"_blank\">My Infinite Macabre Goodies</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/4372-parasite-eve-the-third-birthday-chronicle\" target=\"_blank\">Parasite Eve: The Third Birthday Chronicle</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/899558-shamelessly-pimping-my-book\" target=\"_blank\">Shamelessly pimping my book</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/831-erikmodi","name":"ErikModi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-12T13:32:20-08:00","id":310510,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ErikModi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/224619-what-do-you-think-a-hunter-the-vigil-chronicle-book-should-have?p=310407#post310407\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <b>I'm not saying that Advanced Armory is &quot;core&quot; to their identity, but it is <i>part</i> of it. You play a TF:V Hunter because A) you like bring part of a government agency hunting monsters, B) you like the Storytelling aspects of governmental bureaucracy interfering with helping people, C) you want to have a Stark Industries raygun. Letting everyone buy from Stark Industries steals part of the identity of this specific group, in the same way that everyone being able to use demon powers messes with the Lucifuge and anyone being able to graft monster parts into their bodies messes with Cheiron Group. It's not that they'll have &quot;no&quot; identity if their Endowments are available to everyone, but that part of that identity will be lost, and unless something equally interesting crops up to replace it, all of them will be damaged.</b><br /> <br /> <b>This character, I feel, would be lost were all Endowments available to all groups.</b><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b><u>I'd still say that the Compact doesn't have access to the same kinds of research and development that a funded Federal agency does, but they could come up with some pretty wicked ad hoc solutions that would have their own individual character. Some items might be the same (both could easily create the sunlight flash-bangs), but instead of the Mjolnir Cannon the SWAT team perhaps weapons less overtly destructive, but more tailored to individual threats. Perhaps a weapon with different firing modes or ammo loads designed to exploit the weaknesses of different types of supernatural.</u></b><br /> <br /> Now, that's not to say that Compacts can't be &quot;sponsored&quot; by Conspiracies, kind of as &quot;seed teams&quot; from which to draw talent. In this case, a Cell or Compact could have access to a Conspiracies Endowments because that Conspiracy is funding them, but keeping them separate for some reason.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> And I feel it adds character and flavor to those groups. Lucifuge with Mjolnir Cannons and MM members with demonic powers just seems off to me. I'd rather see the gameplay mechanics continue to reinforce every group's unique character and flavor, then try and handwave away how you can be an AKD member who doesn't bother hunting artifacts because he's got a raygun, or an MM member who still claims he's doing God's work while summoning demons, or a government employee who goes into dangerous situations doped to the gills on a near-fatal concoction.<br /> <br /> And what. . . no love for my Mjolnir Cannon pun? Come on, guys, I worked hard on that one!</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Again, I agree with all of this. Erik hit the nail on the head. I'd love that each conspiracy and/or compact has their own flavor and identity and I like that each of them has their own endowments and character traits specific to their group. If I want to play a military like character that has access to advances weaponry, I'll play TF:V. If I want to play a Hunter with a demonic background, I'll play a Lucifuge. I do think that perhaps a way for a compact to gain access to some of the things that the conspiracies have access to would be cool, as well. But it would have to be in special circumstances. <br /> <br /> I think a few of you are suggesting changes that would drastically alter what I love about Hunter in the first place. I only hope that whomever takes up the development duties on Hunter 2E knows what should and should not stay. Most of what is there already works perfectly fine. Minor changes(and I mean MINOR), with GMC rules update would be just fine.<br /> <br /> Don't fix what isn't broken, IMO.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-13T08:57:04-08:00","id":311332,"title":"","content":"Some thoughts.<br /> <br /> <b>RE: Endowment Availability </b><br /> <br /> What may be a good option is to create a merit that allows a Hunter to gain an endowment from an organization they aren't officially part of (similar to some of the merits being proposed for VtR's <b>Secrets of the Covenants </b>open development). This way, it enables concepts that include some cross-pollination. (such as a Hunter that got abducted by parties unknown and released with few memories and some..thing..inside their body).<br /> <br /> <b>RE: Cells, Compacts, And Conspiracies</b><br /> <br /> What I would like to see is the clarification between the in-game scope of the organization and the scope of the playstyle. Like other here, I would like to see a bit more flexibility in how an particular organization is presented, so it becomes possible to have Cell-Level play with Conspiracy level Organizations.<br /> <br /> <b>RE: Organization Flavor and Background.</b><br /> <br /> So far in second editions, most of the main splats have had their flavor tweaked and revised. I would expect the Hunter Orgs to get a similar treatment. I agree that each of the organizations needs a sharper focus on who they are and what they do now rather than the long write up of overall history.<br /> <br /> Personally, out of all the organizations, I hope the AKD gets a pretty big re-write. I like the flavor of Relic hunters, but I find the animosity with Mages and Werewolves to be kind of forced and awkward. A slight shift of flavor to make them hunters of cursed and dangerous bygones, relics and artifacts as a central theme would be welcome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1420009-the-artificer-s-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">The Artificer's Workshop</a> - A collection of Exalted Artifacts<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806809-curios-relics-and-tomes\" target=\"_blank\">Curios, Relics, and Tomes</a> - A collection of Relics (Cursed and Otherwise)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show\" target=\"_blank\">The Horror Lab</a> - A collection of Beasts, Monsters and less definable things.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1128197-strange-places#post1128197\" target=\"_blank\">Strange Places</a> - A collection of Dark, Mysterious, and Wondrous Locations<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie\" target=\"_blank\">Twilight Menagerie</a> - A collection of Ephemeral Entities","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","name":"Reighnhell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar775_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"749"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-13T09:28:33-08:00","id":311353,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reighnhell</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/224619-what-do-you-think-a-hunter-the-vigil-chronicle-book-should-have?p=311332#post311332\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally, out of all the organizations, I hope the AKD gets a pretty big re-write. I like the flavor of Relic hunters, but I find the animosity with Mages and Werewolves to be kind of forced and awkward. A slight shift of flavor to make them hunters of cursed and dangerous bygones, relics and artifacts as a central theme would be welcome.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's funny, I found the AKD's issues with Mages and Werewolves as a natural outgrowth of their &quot;artifact-hunting&quot; base premise. Since Mages and Werewolves also have hunting down mystical items (albeit of distinctly different flavors) as a large part of what they do, it naturally places them into conflict with AKD.<br /> <br /> I also think that shifting their focus to specifically &quot;cursed&quot; items, or things that are just too dangerous to be out in the world, a little too narrow. It's already difficult to avoid Warehouse 13 comparisons (not that that's necessarily a bad thing), and the cool thing about the AKD is you might very well have an otherwise insurmountable problem until some old archivist type smiles and says &quot;you know, I have just the thing. . .&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/4411-my-geist-gmc-updates\" target=\"_blank\">My Geist GMC Updates</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/4348-my-infinite-macabre-goodies\" target=\"_blank\">My Infinite Macabre Goodies</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/4372-parasite-eve-the-third-birthday-chronicle\" target=\"_blank\">Parasite Eve: The Third Birthday Chronicle</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/899558-shamelessly-pimping-my-book\" target=\"_blank\">Shamelessly pimping my book</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/831-erikmodi","name":"ErikModi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-13T09:45:00-08:00","id":311390,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ErikModi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/224619-what-do-you-think-a-hunter-the-vigil-chronicle-book-should-have?p=311353#post311353\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's funny, I found the AKD's issues with Mages and Werewolves as a natural outgrowth of their &quot;artifact-hunting&quot; base premise. Since Mages and Werewolves also have hunting down mystical items (albeit of distinctly different flavors) as a large part of what they do, it naturally places them into conflict with AKD.<br /> <br /> I also think that shifting their focus to specifically &quot;cursed&quot; items, or things that are just too dangerous to be out in the world, a little too narrow. It's already difficult to avoid Warehouse 13 comparisons (not that that's necessarily a bad thing), and the cool thing about the AKD is you might very well have an otherwise insurmountable problem until some old archivist type smiles and says &quot;you know, I have just the thing. . .&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>This I see a bit more. It makes any conflict more pragmatic than &quot;your people did X back in the dawn of history&quot;. And gives a great way to add Mummies to the dance.<br /> <br /> As far as narrowing the focus, I imagine that the AKD would also run across a good number of benign or useful enough to offset any drawbacks items that their agents would use in the field.<br /> <br /> ..which raises the question of where they keep all this stuff...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1420009-the-artificer-s-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">The Artificer's Workshop</a> - A collection of Exalted Artifacts<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806809-curios-relics-and-tomes\" target=\"_blank\">Curios, Relics, and Tomes</a> - A collection of Relics (Cursed and Otherwise)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show\" target=\"_blank\">The Horror Lab</a> - A collection of Beasts, Monsters and less definable things.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1128197-strange-places#post1128197\" target=\"_blank\">Strange Places</a> - A collection of Dark, Mysterious, and Wondrous Locations<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie\" target=\"_blank\">Twilight Menagerie</a> - A collection of Ephemeral Entities","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","name":"Reighnhell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar775_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"749"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-13T10:01:19-08:00","id":311404,"title":"","content":"They'd keep them in the Labyrinths, same as anything else. They'd just be easier to find.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Aslo, in regards to the relic hunting, mages and werewolves, I had this entire thing about why the AKD is like that. The answer is paradise lost-or rather, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/224619-what-do-you-think-a-hunter-the-vigil-chronicle-book-should-have?p=227282#post227282\">paradise shattered.</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 11-13-2014, 01:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-13T11:16:38-08:00","id":311479,"title":"","content":"So, I have a few comments and ideas.<br /> AKD and mummies make almost too much sense to be ignored, but I don't see an inherent conflict. AKD has been around for a very long time, I think its very likely they know about and have operational information on Mummies. I mean the AKD might even have a few Mummy members, if the Iremite can remember. The AKD also have a unique perspective among hunter groups, they play the super long game. Their goal is to gather more relics and punish the things that broke the world which is similar enough to the Mummy goal that they likely agree on a number of things.<br /> <br /> Endowments and tiers should be tied to one another. I think every compact and every conspiracy should have their own set of endowments. I also believe endowments should scale with tier, with T3 having the biggest, baddest things available. Each tier of endowments includes the lower tier's things. This method ensures that at each level of play every compact/conspiracy means something other than a filled in blank spot. This of course assumes that tiers are rewritten as scope of play and that we abolish compact and conspiracy being tied to tiers and let folks play their chosen group at any level.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2861-nyx","name":"Nyx","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2861_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-13T18:31:01-08:00","id":311831,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyx</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/224619-what-do-you-think-a-hunter-the-vigil-chronicle-book-should-have?p=311479#post311479\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, I have a few comments and ideas.<br /> AKD and mummies make almost too much sense to be ignored, but I don't see an inherent conflict. AKD has been around for a very long time, I think its very likely they know about and have operational information on Mummies. I mean the AKD might even have a few Mummy members, if the Iremite can remember. The AKD also have a unique perspective among hunter groups, they play the super long game. Their goal is to gather more relics and punish the things that broke the world which is similar enough to the Mummy goal that they likely agree on a number of things.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I wouldn't be surprised if a few Deceived were on call. Not within the ranks mind you (after all, not all of the relics that AKD have related to Irem but a good percent do) as they don't share the whole &quot;Kill civilization because we were cheated out of our due!&quot; mindset but as useful contacts who can scratch each others backs.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-13T18:35:57-08:00","id":311834,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Not really. To me the core of the Lucifuge is about the inner demon. Shock didn't describe how to capture that with pure mortals - nor do I really think the Lucifuge is the appropriate place for it. It's one specific way of looking at inner demons, (the Loyalists of Thule are another) it would be hard to make it work without the actual genetic heratage. </div> </div> </div>The answer is simple. Have Possessed in the Lucifuge.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-13T20:09:43-08:00","id":311878,"title":"","content":"Well\u2026 yes, and no. I\u2019m certainly not opposed to having the Possessed in the ranks of the Lucifuge; but neither do I think that every member of the org that isn\u2019t a Child of the Seventh Generation is instead Possessed \u2014 indeed, Possessed members ought to be rare. As well, the whole point of the exercise is to feature the Lucifuge org in chronicles where the protagonists don\u2019t have Supernatural Merits. <br /> <br /> Fortunately, I also don\u2019t buy the argument that the only valid way to play the Lucifuge org is \u201cstruggling with your inner demon\u201d. Yes, that\u2019s the way to play those who have the org\u2019s Endowment; but without it, the focus shifts to \u201cfighting the demonic\u201d, with an emphasis on supporting/monitoring those with demonic tendencies who are fighting said tendencies. If you don\u2019t find that compelling, fine; it\u2019s you prerogative not to feature any Lucifuge who don\u2019t have its Endowment.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-13T20:33:52-08:00","id":311893,"title":"","content":"I don't feel like going hardcore into the Lucifuge despite them being my favorite cause ahm tired. But that said, the themes of the organization are heritage and circumstance versus choice, namely summarized as compassionate determination of monstrous standing(The Denial are redeemers, but most of the Lucifuge has some inclination towards it, cause if they can fight off evil, anyone else can) and fighting fire with fire(The Reconciliation stands as a group representative, but by and large a group that grabs the forces of evil to fight evil has to be considered such).<br /> <br /> Also Data, while I recognize that character can be a member of these organizations without the endowments, trying to divorce Endowments from purpose is silly, <i>particularly</i> for the Lucifuge. Endowments are a huge part of the culture and the direction of any organization that has them. Humans beings are tool using creatures-we build our entire society around them, and that's going to go double for the Conspiracies. Trying to divorce the Lucifuge from Castigations or Task Force Valkyrie from Advanced Armory as a whole is castration, pure and simple.<br /> <br /> On a final note, one does not need to summon hellfire to have inner demons. Even if a Lucifuge has no Castigations, the entire idea of the organization is that, as a member of a demonic heritage, you have to deal with abnormaly strong unsavory urges.<br /> <br /> Individual characters choices do not shape the whole of an organization. Even people by themselves don't wholly do that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 11-16-2014, 02:24 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-14T12:04:31-08:00","id":312470,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/224619-what-do-you-think-a-hunter-the-vigil-chronicle-book-should-have?p=311404#post311404\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">EDIT: Aslo, in regards to the relic hunting, mages and werewolves, I had this entire thing about why the AKD is like that. The answer is paradise lost-or rather, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/224619-what-do-you-think-a-hunter-the-vigil-chronicle-book-should-have?p=227282#post227282\">paradise shattered.</a></div> </div> </div> </div>And as I said back then - Irem has more influence on Mummy's present day activities than Pangaia has on Werewolves present day activities which makes Mummies a better opponent for a paradise shattered theme even without thinking about Relics.<br /> <br /> I still think that the AKD need a more interesting way to relate to their paradise lost than killing monsters. I want to see them with grand plans to restore their lost paradise, monsters just get in their way.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/224619-what-do-you-think-a-hunter-the-vigil-chronicle-book-should-have?p=311893#post311893\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But that said, the themes of the organization are heritage and circumstance versus choice, namely summarized as compassionate determination of monstrous standing(The Denial are redeemers, but most of the Lucifuge has some inclination towards it, cause if they can fight off evil, anyone else can) and fighting fire with fire(The Reconciliation stands as a group representative, but by and large a group that grabs the forces of evil to fight evil has to be considered such).</div> </div> </div> </div>I always saw the three groups as about how you see yourself.<br /> <br /> The Denial: I'm not a monster! I'm a hunter, I just have a monster ancestor.<br /> The Reconciliation: Yeah, I'm a monster. Doesn't mean I'm a bad person.<br /> The Truth: I don't actually know what I am, but I'm going to find out.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-14T12:16:06-08:00","id":312477,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/224619-what-do-you-think-a-hunter-the-vigil-chronicle-book-should-have?p=312470#post312470\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And as I said back then -</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, plenty of other people have already pointed out the problem with your perspective. I might actually tie it all up, but for now there's that. On tying to paradise shattered, what do you think the relics are for? It's really not just collection.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I always saw the three groups as about how you see yourself.<br /> <br /> The Denial: I'm not a monster! I'm a hunter, I just have a monster ancestor.<br /> The Reconciliation: Yeah, I'm a monster. Doesn't mean I'm a bad person.<br /> The Truth: I don't actually know what I am, but I'm going to find out.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not a bad shot at it. My own associations were incidental to a different tangent, so having this as an explicit look at the groups is good.<br /> <br /> Of course, the thing of the matter is that the Denial and Truth are the 'nice' guys of the bunch. The Reconciliation is less likely to be since they can redeem the whole world by removing Satan's anchors, which they translate to monsters. They're the ones of the Lucifuge most likely to just straight up kill a monster.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-14T13:15:59-08:00","id":312500,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/224619-what-do-you-think-a-hunter-the-vigil-chronicle-book-should-have?p=312477#post312477\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, plenty of other people have already pointed out the problem with your perspective. I might actually tie it all up, but for now there's that.</div> </div> </div> </div> Whom are you refering too? Michael? He agreed with me on Pangea which is probably the most important point in the Mage/Werewolf/Mummy thing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/224619-what-do-you-think-a-hunter-the-vigil-chronicle-book-should-have?p=312477#post312477\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On tying to paradise shattered, what do you think the relics are for? It's really not just collection.</div> </div> </div> </div> Are you referring to the bit about the leaders wanting their magic back? If not then I don't know what you mean.<br /> <br /> Personally I'd like the reason they're collecting Relics to be a lot more promiment in the organisation - my prefered reason is rebuilding the civilsation they lost and reclaiming their powers. To the point that the Big Plan can serve as the typical motivation for an AKD hunter instead of a burning hatered against certain splats.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/224619-what-do-you-think-a-hunter-the-vigil-chronicle-book-should-have?p=312477#post312477\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Of course, the thing of the matter is that the Denial and Truth are the 'nice' guys of the bunch. The Reconciliation is less likely to be since they can redeem the whole world by removing Satan's anchors, which they translate to monsters. They're the ones of the Lucifuge most likely to just straight up kill a monster.</div> </div> </div> </div>I never liked that angle; I think my portrayal is accurate to the corebook's write up and I feel that later books really screwed up by permemently tying the faction with the explicitly positive self-identity to fanaticism. Someone who knows that their heratage is terrible yet still finds something positive in it is a charachter full of potential and that should not have been promoted instead of buried.<br /> <br /> Lucifuge fanatics are fine - but fanaticism and Faction affiliation should be independent.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-14T14:21:33-08:00","id":312544,"title":"","content":"I think the Lucifuge strongly needed the Reconciliation to be written as the fatalistic, mystical monster slayers.The other two branches serve to humanize the organization; they're hunters who are easy to relate to and understand. Denial and Truth echo questions that every day people ask, &quot;Who am I?&quot;, &quot;What does it mean to be human?&quot;. Only Reconciliation asks something a little bit different, &quot;How far would I go to erase evil from the world?&quot;. Not every facet of every Organization should be something that is easy to relate to. These groups have lived in shadow and secret, fighting things that shouldn't exist for (in some cases) centuries. They should not be completely understandable or graspable. Killing to redeem the devil is a great example.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2861-nyx","name":"Nyx","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2861_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-14T14:53:01-08:00","id":312590,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/224619-what-do-you-think-a-hunter-the-vigil-chronicle-book-should-have?p=312500#post312500\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally I'd like the reason they're collecting Relics to be a lot more promiment in the organisation -</div> </div> </div> </div>You are really not paying attention to the organization if you can't see that everything you're asking them to do <i>is already being done</i>. It's not ignored, it's all over the damned text.<br /> <br /> This also ties into why they need to hunt the people who ruined it in the first place down.<br /> <br /> And on an unrelated note, Pangaea alone is not the most important point in that argument.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Also, Nyx knows where it's at.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-14T15:02:34-08:00","id":312597,"title":"","content":"@Nix<br /> <br /> I don't think your point and mine are actually in conflict. There's room in the Lucifuge for both hunters who see something positive in their heritage and for weird ideas like killing to redeem the devil. What I think is wrong is tying the two togeather. Hunters who see something positive in their heratage shouldn't be limited to having weird and murderous ideas; and there's also room for weird and murderous ideas in the Denial.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/224619-what-do-you-think-a-hunter-the-vigil-chronicle-book-should-have?p=312590#post312590\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You are really not paying attention to the organization if you can't see that everything you're asking them to do <i>is already being done</i>. It's not ignored, it's all over the damned text.</div> </div> </div> </div>Then please, page numbers.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 11-14-2014, 06:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-15T11:02:48-08:00","id":313087,"title":"","content":"I hope they de-skeeve Ashwood Abbey. <br /> <br /> Because seriously, its really skeevy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3738-illuminated-minutia","name":"Illuminated Minutia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3738_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-16T07:01:38-08:00","id":313659,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Illuminated Minutia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/224619-what-do-you-think-a-hunter-the-vigil-chronicle-book-should-have?p=313087#post313087\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I hope they de-skeeve Ashwood Abbey.<br /> <br /> Because seriously, its really skeevy.</div> </div> </div> </div>But that's what I love about it! If you don't want to be a sickening degenerate, go join the Union <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/4411-my-geist-gmc-updates\" target=\"_blank\">My Geist GMC Updates</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/4348-my-infinite-macabre-goodies\" target=\"_blank\">My Infinite Macabre Goodies</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/4372-parasite-eve-the-third-birthday-chronicle\" target=\"_blank\">Parasite Eve: The Third Birthday Chronicle</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/899558-shamelessly-pimping-my-book\" target=\"_blank\">Shamelessly pimping my book</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/831-erikmodi","name":"ErikModi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-16T08:45:00-08:00","id":313747,"title":"","content":"I wouldn't remove the skeve; but I would make it clear that Abbey is about novelty - trying to do stuff you haven't ever done before because you're board. Sometimes that leads to you trying ever more pererted stuff, other times it doesn't.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-16T10:28:46-08:00","id":313838,"title":"","content":"I think that viable way of playing 2ed Hunter should be to &quot;leave the Conspiracy away but left with your own Endowments&quot;. Like lone, Task Force VALKYRIE officer that lives in his little town in the middle of nowhere. So yeah, I'm all about decoupling Endowments with Tier of character.<br /> <br /> BTW: How to solve multiple Tier characters in one play? Like one is from Lone Night, other is from VALKIRYE, and another is unaffiliated?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 11-18-2014, 04:39 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-17T17:18:47-08:00","id":314947,"title":"","content":"Well that's the real benefit of decoupling the organizations from tiers. It will make every group applicable to every desired level of play. No organization is restricted to a tier, because tiers become an indicator of